{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/178995-what-s-your-custom-kiths","id":178995,"title":"What's YOUR Custom Kiths?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-06-24T09:53:01-07:00","id":178995,"title":"What's YOUR Custom Kiths?","content":"So yeah, I'm curious to see what sort of fan made Kiths (if any) you guys have come up with for Changeling the Lost. Below are a handful of my personal creations. Would also appreciate some feed back to see if the powers I gave them are any good. I'm not sure if I made them too OP or not.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <u>Ogre Kiths</u><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Ashura:</b> A culture themed Kith of low ranking demigods who are known to possess 3 faces and six arms.<br /> <br /> Blessing - Effortless Multitasking: By spending Glamour, the Changeling can produce additional limbs for the remainder of the scene that enables them to perform up to 3 separate actions at the same time without suffering any penalties for dividing their attention. In combat, this can also be used to perform up to 3 simultaneous attacks in the same turn.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Greatbeards:</b> Sea fairing Ogres who were used for pirating during their time in Arcadia. Their name is derived from such beings as Blackbeard, Whitebeard, Bluebeard, Redbeard, Brownbeard, and so on.<br /> <br /> Blessing - Captain on Deck: By spending Glamour, the Greatbeard can enhance their commanding presence to rally their allies and intimidate their foes. For the rest of the scene, the Changeling gains +2 to Charisma and Intimidation, as if they were a pirate captain leading the assault on an enemy vessel!<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <u>Beast Kiths</u><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Tough Hides:</b> Tortoises, shellfish, and other beasts with armored plating instead of exposed flesh.<br /> <br /> Blessing - Armored Shell: By spending Glamour, the Changeling can fortify themselves with natural armor. The amount of armor they gain is equal to the amount of Glamour they spend (+1 armor for 1 Glamour, +2 for 2, est). The armor bonus lasts for the remainder of the scene.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Hunting Hounds:</b> Expert trackers who hunted down fellow Changelings for sport during their time in Arcadia. Often plagued with guilt after escaping, and distrusted by their fellow Changelings because of their deeds.<br /> <br /> Blessing - Tracker's Nose: By spending Glamour and sniffing a person or their belongings, the Changeling can memorize their scent. From then on, they can track their location by smell, which comes in clear even over various other scents in the area. The subject must have been in the area within the last 48 hours or the scent goes cold for that location.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Nightmares:</b> Equines who were used to transport their masters through the dreams of mortals during their time in Arcadia. After their escape, they found they have a higher affinity for the dream world than most Changelings.<br /> <br /> Blessing - Dreamwalker's Natural Habitat: The Nightmare gains +2 on any attempts to use offensive powers while in the dream world.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <u>Darkling Kiths</u><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Shells:</b> Completely traumatized by their time in Arcadia, these Changelings have forgotten how to express their emotions. Social introverts, they find it even more difficult to associate with others than normal.<br /> <br /> Blessing - Roll with the Pain: By spending Glamour and touching a subject, the Shell is able to render them extremely resilient to trauma by suppressing their ability to feel. For the duration of this power (rest of the scene), the subject is granted a bonus of +1 Willpower for each point of Glamour spent on them. This Willpower can be spent like normal Willpower points, but all of the bestowed Willpower will vanish after the scene, potentially draining the subject of all remaining Willpower if they are careless with its use! The downside to this power is that because the subject is emotionally suppressed, you can not harvest Glamour from them while they are under its effects.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <u>Fairest Kiths</u><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Concubine:</b> Forced into the sex trade during their time in Arcadia, these Fairest have learned how to use their sex appeal as a weapon to coax others into dropping their guard.<br /> <br /> Blessing - Royal Consort: By spending Glamour, the Concubine can make those around them more susceptible to their advances, as they find it easier to trust the Changeling and open up to them. For the duration of the scene, the Concubine gets a bonus of +2 to all persuasion and seduction rolls. Additionally, this bonus applies to the next attack they perform against that subject (treated as a surprise attack). However, attacking a subject instantly negates the power and can not be reused against them for the next 72 hours.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <u>Wizened Kiths</u><br /> <br /> <b>Pixie:</b> The remains of children who were abducted by the Gentry when they were too young to fully understood what happened to them. Becoming mischievous pranksters after their escape. they now amuse themselves at the expense of others.<br /> <br /> Blessing - Child's Play: By spending Glamour, the Pixie is able to construct a booby trap (they call it a Prank) which will be set off when someone fulfills the condition to activate it (stepping on a wire, opening a container, est). The more Glamour they spend, the more complicated the prank can be from as simple as a can of powder, to cartoonishly rigging an entire room with a series of complex gadgets.<br /> <br /> For each point of Glamour spent, the Pixie can rig 1 additional step to the trap, as well as increase its damage potential (Bashing or Lethal) by +1. So by spending 3 Glamour, they could rig a trap that has 3 steps to it, and inflicts 3 points of either Bashing or Lethal damage. For every 2 steps the trap is comprised of, it takes 1 round to hit. So a 1 step trap would hit instantly, a 2-3 step trap would take 1 round, a 4-5 step trap would take 2 rounds, and so on.<br /> <br /> <br /> Additional Effects and Costs<br /> <br /> Poison - +1 Glamour equal to its potency<br /> <br /> Blind (2 rounds) - +2 Glamour<br /> <br /> Deafen (2 Rounds) - +2 Glamour<br /> <br /> Knock Down (1 Round) +1 Glamour for Small, +2 for Medium, +3 for Large targets<br /> <br /> Unconscious - +1 Glamour equal to amount of hours desired. Subject can be forcefully awoken by special means.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 06-24-2014, 02:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-24T10:12:01-07:00","id":179017,"title":"","content":"Off the top of my head, a lot of these seem overpowered if only because they scale-remember, most kith blessings are around +2, +3 for those that only come up in really specific circumstances. Concubines and Greatbeards, with their kith bonuses set to flat +2, would look balanced to me. I can't remember the name off the top of my head but I think there's already a Beast kith that grants armor, and 2 per dot of Wyrd is absurd-at Wyrd 3 that lets you spend 1 Glamour and effectively be invincible for a scene unless the GM starts throwing explosions around. Nightmares also get too much of a bonus-even at only +2, a flat bonus to <i>all actions taken in dreams </i>just seems OP to me.<br /> Hunting Hounds are a good idea, although I don't think you need to make them pay another Glamour to continue tracking a scent.<br /> <br /> My favorites of these thematically are the Shell and the Pixie, both of which I think need their blessings redone. The Pixie's blessing needs at least some damage/Glamour expenditure guidelines, and the Shell blessing is useless to anyone without derangements. Maybe Shell's blessing could be something Willpower-focused?<br /> <br /> I drew up one or two Beast kiths a while ago while I was bored, let me see if I can find them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2709-quatrevingts","name":"QuatreVingts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2709_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"55"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-24T10:20:40-07:00","id":179024,"title":"","content":"<b>Tamers</b><b>:</b> These Fairest spent their Durances in the keep of animalistic Fae, the Belle to some horrid B\u00eate, or perhaps forced to hone their natural charisma toward keeping a herd of mangy hobgoblins in line. Their Blessing is <i>Soothing the Savage</i>: the changeling can spend Glamour to improve Animal Ken rolls on a one-for-one basis, and gains the 9-again quality on any social rolls made against animals or the sufficiently-animal-like (such as hobgoblins of the proper kind, animal spirits, and, much to their chagrin, consternation, and dismay, changelings of the Beast Seeming).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-24T10:25:51-07:00","id":179025,"title":"","content":"<b>Fairest Maiden: </b>Stolen to Arcadia to serve as the prize in contests and the object of quests, maidens shine with beauty and innocence. All attempts to see the bad in a Maiden, such as contesting her Subterfuge roll to claim innocence, and all attempts to convince others of a Maiden's misdeeds take a -2 penalty.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-24T10:38:20-07:00","id":179038,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>QuatreVingts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/178995-what-s-your-custom-kiths?p=179017#post179017\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Off the top of my head, a lot of these seem overpowered if only because they scale-remember, most kith blessings are around +2, +3 for those that only come up in really specific circumstances. Concubines and Greatbeards, with their kith bonuses set to flat +2, would look balanced to me. I can't remember the name off the top of my head but I think there's already a Beast kith that grants armor, and 2 per dot of Wyrd is absurd-at Wyrd 3 that lets you spend 1 Glamour and effectively be invincible for a scene unless the GM starts throwing explosions around. Nightmares also get too much of a bonus-even at only +2, a flat bonus to <i>all actions taken in dreams </i>just seems OP to me.<br /> Hunting Hounds are a good idea, although I don't think you need to make them pay another Glamour to continue tracking a scent.<br /> <br /> My favorites of these thematically are the Shell and the Pixie, both of which I think need their blessings redone. The Pixie's blessing needs at least some damage/Glamour expenditure guidelines, and the Shell blessing is useless to anyone without derangements. Maybe Shell's blessing could be something Willpower-focused?<br /> <br /> I drew up one or two Beast kiths a while ago while I was bored, let me see if I can find them.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Actually, I was thinking the Hounds spend extra Glamour to recall that scent at later dates, not immediately afterward. But I suppose I should tone down the armor.<br /> <br /> As for the damage on Pixie traps, I was thinking more along the lines of letting the ST or the rule book handle that. For example, if they made an exploding present, its damage would be accounted by what type of bomb it would function as. Same thing for attaching nails to a baseball bat and rigging it onto a rotating pipe to club the victim in the chest. It would depend more on what they made, rather than how they made it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I'll go back and tone down some of these, thank you for the advice. Maybe for Nightmares, I'll make it a bonus to using offensive powers, since they're pretty much named after hurtful dreams, after all.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> EDIT: Alright, I went back and fixed a lot of them, including Pixie traps. What do you think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 06-24-2014, 01:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-24T11:12:47-07:00","id":179078,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/178995-what-s-your-custom-kiths?p=179038#post179038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually, I was thinking the Hounds spend extra Glamour to recall that scent at later dates, not immediately afterward. But I suppose I should tone down the armor.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>IMO spending one Glamour to memorize a scent is enough, or maybe spending one Glamour just enhances their sense of smell for a scene?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/178995-what-s-your-custom-kiths?p=179038#post179038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As for the damage on Pixie traps, I was thinking more along the lines of letting the ST or the rule book handle that. For example, if they made an exploding present, its damage would be accounted by what type of bomb it would function as. Same thing for attaching nails to a baseball bat and rigging it onto a rotating pipe to club the victim in the chest. It would depend more on what they made, rather than how they made it.</div> </div> </div> </div>You'll want some guidelines on Glamour costs though. Maybe a flat one Glamour to set a trap that effectively attacks with a custom dice pool (probably Wits+Crafts or something), one more Glamour to make a trap that deals lethal damage, one more to incorporate poison or explosive components?<br /> <br /> Here's the only one I could find:<br /> <br /> <i>Beast: </i>The <b>Raucous </b>are made in the image of the Steller's Jay, the Howler Monkey, the Cicada, and other animals that are heard more than they are seen. Among Changelings of the San Fransisco Bay Area, Raucous Beasts made in the image of birds are sometimes referred to as <i>Telegraphs</i>. Their <i>Incessant Chatter </i>can prove a lifesaving distraction: one of the Raucous may spend a point of Glamour at any time they can speak to begin prattling on endlessly about something at most tangentially related to the conversation at hand. One enemy within earshot (who must be selected when the Chatter begins) suffers a -2 penalty to all Mental rolls <i>or </i>to all combat rolls while the Beast continues to chatter; once a choice has been made, the penalty cannot be reallocated until the Changeling activates this power again. If the Raucous is prevented from speaking, this power immediately ends.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2709-quatrevingts","name":"QuatreVingts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2709_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"55"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-24T11:26:22-07:00","id":179082,"title":"","content":"There, I added an Additional Effects and Cost pool, and edited the Hunting Hounds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-24T13:24:02-07:00","id":179194,"title":"","content":"Not a new, but redone. Draggone: once per scene the changeling can spend a point of glamour and make a ranged breath attack against one opponent. The attack is Presence + Stamina vs Defense (only supernatural armor works against it) and does supernatural lethal damage; Short range is Wyrd in yards.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-24T14:00:40-07:00","id":179216,"title":"","content":"Got some more. ^_^<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Scarred Ones:</b> Tortured to death and revived an uncountable number of times during their stay in Arcadia, these crazed Ogres no longer fear death in any form! Their bodies are often marked by hundreds of scars, as if they were sewn back together!<br /> <br /> Blessing - Wouldn't be the First Time: Having experienced countless tortures at the hands of the True Fae, the Scarred Ones have extremely high pain thresholds. By spending Glamour, they can negate Wound Penalties on a 1 for 1 payment<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Beverages:</b> These liquid Elementals were turned into drinks to satiate the thirst of their masters. Milk, wine, beer, est, they still carry the touch of their durances in their veins.<br /> <br /> Blessing - Quenching Blood: By spending Glamour and cutting themselves, the Elemental can transmute their own blood into a certain type of drink. If consumed, their blood will not only quench a person's thirst, but also transfer the spent Glamour over to them. The amount of Glamour spent determines how much is transferred. Using this power causes 1 lethal damage, plus an additional +1 lethal for every 2 extra Glamour spent. So spending 3 Glamour would inflict 2 Lethal damage upon the Beverage.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Traders:</b> Wizened who were placed in charge of their master's financial accounts, or whatever passed for such in Arcadia. Legendary investors, bankers, and merchants, they have a knack for acquiring wealth.<br /> <br /> Blessing - Midas Touch: By spending Glamour and touching an inanimate object, the Banker can vastly improve its market value. When attempting to sell or trade the designated object, they get a +2 on all rolls involving haggling or persuasion.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Imp:</b> Child sized devils who are the remains of unruly children. It is speculated that the Gentry may have believed their parents did not do a proper job disciplining them, but no conclusive proof has been found to support this. Their time spent in Arcadia has turned these wizened into vulgar brats, who manage to effortlessly goad others into violent outbursts.<br /> <br /> Blessing - Little Hellspawn: The Imps are infamous for their disrespect and improper conduct. By spending a point of Glamour, the Imp can perform a display that is so insulting, their target loses the ability to think straight and becomes more prone to violence. The subject must roll a save of Wits + Composure to avoid falling for the trick, but as long as the Imp continues to spend Glamour, they can maintain the display until their subject finally snaps! The cost of using this blessing is 1 Glamour for each target they attempt to effect for that turn (3 targets would require the spending of 3 Glamour).<br /> <br /> Subjects who fall for the Imp's display suffer a -2 on all social and mental rolls for the rest of the scene, but receive a +2 on all physical actions.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Toon:</b> A culture themed Fairest who's beauty is depicted in popular cartoon series, more specifically Japanese anime. Supernaturally gifted warriors, they can withstand unbelievable levels of abuse before falling in battle. Their durances were often spent providing entertainment for their Keepers in the form of TV and comic book characters. How the Gentry came to learn about cartoons and comics is anyone's guess.<br /> <br /> Blessing - Cartoon Violence: in many popular cartoons, the characters are seen to endure attacks which would pulverize most humans, and yet get right back up and continue the fight. These Fairest are able to mimic this level of resilience to a certain degree. By spending Glamour, a Toon can soak 1 point of damage on a 1 for 2 cost (spending 4 Glamour soaks 2 damage, est). This power lasts for a number of attacks equal to half their Wyrd, up to a maximum of 5 attacks at level 10, minimum of 1 attack at level 1.<br /> <br /> When it wears off, they must spend Glamour again to reactivate it, or their protection will fade and they become vulnerable again. Once they spend the Glamour they are stuck with that amount of protection until it wears off. Meaning they can not spend 3, and then upgrade it to 5 before the 3 wears off.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Minotaur:</b> The bull headed wardens of labyrinths, dungeons, and mazes. These Ogres were used as jail keepers to prevent their fellow Changelings from escaping Arcadia. Ironically being prisoners themselves, their freedom came on the day they accidentally stumbled upon the hidden exit during patrol.<br /> <br /> <br /> Blessing - Dungeon Master: Having spent so much time patrolling halls and corridors, the Minotaur has manifested a 6th sense when it comes to finding their way around. By spending a point of Glamour, the Minotaur gains a +2 on attempts to navigate any indoor structure. They have a subconscious awareness of the location of everyone and everything. This effect lasts for the remainder of the scene, or until the Minotaur stops spending Glamour to renew it. If the Minotaur steps outside, they likewise deactivate the power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 06-24-2014, 11:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-25T08:05:51-07:00","id":179714,"title":"","content":"<b>Excalibur:</b> Transformed into sentient weapons and wielded by their Keepers throughout many battles, these Elementals have an unrivaled comprehension of how to fight with their former bodies.<br /> <br /> Blessing - Bond of the Master: Having spent time as an actual weapon, the Excalibur has a deeper understanding of how to wield it. At character generation, the Changeling selects 1 specific weapon class and gains a +2 bonus on any attack rolls made with that weapon.<br /> <br /> Class Examples: Short Swords (1 handed), Long Swords (2 handed), Axes (1 handed), Battle Axes (2 handed) Hammers (1 handed), Warhammers (2 handed), Spears, Pole Arms (Staff), Clubs, Maces, Daggers, Bow &amp; Arrow, Crossbow<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Gorgon:</b> Mortals who were so beautiful, they offended an envious Gentry. These Ogres have been twisted into hideous creatures in order to satisfy their Keeper's vanity.<br /> <br /> Blessing - Gaze of Stone: When they were in Arcadia, anyone who looked upon a Gorgon's face would be turned to stone. After their escape, this curse has been greatly weakened, and can even prove beneficial to a cunning Gorgon. By spending Glamour, the Gorgon can inflict paralysis in those who look at their face, lasting for a number of hours equal to how much Glamour is spent. A physical shock (such as pain) can break the spell, however, as the victim is knocked back to their senses.<br /> <br /> The subject must make a composure roll in order to retain their mobility in the face of such a disgusting figure.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Shade:</b> Living embodiments of darkness, these Darklings are virtually impossible to capture at night. They are highly effective spies, assassins, and other covert agents in the Free Holds.<br /> <br /> Blessing - Can't Catch a Shadow: Shades are at one with the darkness itself. When they are standing in a shadow, they can spend Glamour to become incoporeal darkness. They must continue to spend 1 Glamour for each round this blessing remains active.<br /> <br /> The blessing is dispelled by either stopping the Glamour payment, moving outside of the shadow, or banishing the shadow with some kind of light source. While incorporeal, the Shade is immune to conventional attacks, but is likewise restricted in what manner of attacks they can perform.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Tendril Arms:</b> Octopi, Squids, Jellyfish and other forms of tentacled Beasts. The Tendril Arms are naturally talented wrestlers, who have a knack for grappling their opponents into submission.<br /> <br /> <br /> Blessing - Tentacle Hold: The Tendril Arms gain a +3 bonus when attempting a grapple attack. This bonus applies to both initiating the grapple, as well as maintaining it should the subject attempt to break free.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Teddy:</b> These poor bastards were changed into stuffed animals and used as toys for their Keepers to play with. Having endured countless tea parties, playing dress up and other acts of public humiliation and degradation, these Wizened have no tolerance for children and become quickly agitated with anyone who comments on their cute, plushy appearances.<br /> <br /> Blessing - Just a Doll: By spending Glamour, the Teddy can enter a state in which they appear to be an inanimate object, like a common stuffed toy. They are still aware of what goes on around them (making this an effective blessing for spying), but they can not react to their environment. Just a Doll requires they spend 1 Glamour to last for the remainder of the scene.<br /> <br /> The effect can be canceled early to regain their mobility, but costs an additional Glamour to do so. If the Teddy has no Glamour to cancel it, this can leave them extremely vulnerable to attack!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 06-25-2014, 06:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-25T15:01:58-07:00","id":180106,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/178995-what-s-your-custom-kiths?p=179714#post179714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Teddy:</b> These poor bastards were changed into stuffed animals and used as toys for their Keepers to play with. Having endured countless tea parties, playing dress up and other acts of public humiliation and degradation, these Wizened have no tolerance for children and become quickly agitated with anyone who comments on their cute, plushy appearances.<br /> <br /> Blessing - Just a Doll: By spending Glamour, the Teddy can enter a state in which they appear to be an inanimate object, like a common stuffed toy. They are still aware of what goes on around them (making this an effective blessing for spying), but they can not react to their environment. Just a Doll requires they spend 1 Glamour for each round it is maintained, and if the Glamour payment stops, they regain their bodily functions and mobility.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd suggest making it one Glamour to have it last a scene, but it requires another Glamour to be canceled early. Otherwise you're looking at spending 20 Glamour per minute to maintain it, which is insane.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-25T15:12:26-07:00","id":180114,"title":"","content":"Fixed. ^_^<br /> <br /> What do you think of the others?<br /> <br /> <br /> Also went back and changed the Many Arms to Tendril Arms. Their original name made it sound like they would get too complicated in battle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 06-25-2014, 06:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-26T17:11:03-07:00","id":181442,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\">Crossposting from <i>Arkham</i>. I know the Leviathan kith blows the Swimmerskin/Waterborn out of the water, but I really don't think something as situational as &quot;breathe water for a scene&quot; is potent enough to be a whole kith blessing. The Manikin kith was my guideline for the powerlevel on that - very situational bonus, and a cost break on Contracts - and I think it works fine.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Beast</span> </div> </div> </div></span></span><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Leviathan: Beneath the surface of Arcadia\u2019s seas lurk all manner of especially dreadful Fae, dead but dreaming in lightless depths. A Lost taken to such a domain must either learn to breathe water or quickly die, and as such develop The Lungs of a Fish: by spending a point of Glamour, the Leviathan may breathe underwater for the rest of the scene. They may also purchase Contracts of Elements (Water) at a rate of (new dots x5 Experience Points), to reflect their affinity with the brine.</span></span></span></div><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Darkling</span></span></span><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Grotesque: Within Arcadia lurk all manner of hideous or faceless horrors that react with fury to a human visage, shaping flesh like clay into it is horribly distorted. The Lost that suffer such a fate Wear No Mask: by spending a point of Glamour, they may reveal their true face to a single target, inflict a -3 penalty to all rolls for a number of turns equal to the Grotesque\u2019s Wyrd unless they pass a Resolve + Composure roll. The Grotesque may only Wear No Mask once per scene.</span></span></span></div><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Elemental</span></span></span><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Massive: In the cold reaches of space lurk black holes so massive and dense that everything, light included, is drawn into its gravity and crushed beyond any hope of escape. Some Fae lurk in similarly crushing realms (or are massive enough to have this gravity themselves), and impart upon the Massive the gift of Apocalyptic Gravity: by spending a point of Glamour, the Massive may add his Wyrd as a bonus to any rolls made to grapple.</span></span></span></div><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Fairest</span></span></span><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Hierophant: Many Keepers style themselves as deities, demanding those they abduct worship them with proper fervor or suffer immensely. Those who stand out in these cults are elected priests and become Hierophants, gaining the Zealot\u2019s Fervor: the Hierophant gains a +2 bonus to any roll made to rile up a crowd and may spend one Glamour to gain the Inspiring merit for the rest of the scene (if he has the Inspiring merit, then he gains a +1 bonus to that Presence + Socialize roll).</span></span></span></div><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Ogre</span></span></span><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Cancerous: Some portions of Arcadia are pestilent, inhabited by creatures of blight, corruption, and radiation that bring slow death to all but the hardiest of Lost. Those that survive are riddled with growths, gaining the Tumor\u2019s Toughness: the Cancerous may spend a point of Glamour to ignore all wound penalties and penalties caused by pain and discomfort for the rest of the scene. They also gain a +2 bonus to rolls made to resist poisons and disease.</span></span></span></div><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Wizened</span></span></span><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Architect: Many Keepers rely on bizarre mathematics to keep their impossible domains functioning properly, and the understanding of these strange principles is a rare an unpleasant gift indeed. For those who have beheld the cyclopean towers of Arcadia, there is nothing more delightful than the study of Hypergeometry: the Architect gains a +1 bonus to any rolls made to conceal or protect his Hollow. He may also buy the Hollow merit and merits relating to Hollows (Archive, Bastion, etc) at a discounted rate of (new dots x1 Experience Points).</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-26T18:24:58-07:00","id":181491,"title":"","content":"<u>Ogre Kiths</u><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Oafish:</b> The world's strongest creatures are often the stupidest. Lost who became Oafish were given the exclusive task of bashing heads and weren't supposed to think any further beyond that. After having an uncharacteristically high moment of enlightenment, they managed to escape back to the mundane world, but they continue to suffer headaches whenever they try to think too much.<br /> <br /> Blessing - Brawn over Brains: When it comes to talents, the Oafish are far more gifted to brute strength than cognitive functions. An Oafish is able to buy Physical attributes at 1/3 the normal experience cost and physical skills at 1/2 the normal cost. However attempting to purchase Mental attributes costs 3x as much experience, and attempting to purchase mental skills costs 4x as much<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Juggernaut:</b> Living wrecking balls, the Juggernauts are Lost who became nearly unstoppable forces on the battlefield. Plowing through enemy ranks with enough force to send people flying, only a fool would stand between these Ogres and their target.<br /> <br /> Blessing - Unstoppable Force: By spending a point of Glamour, the Juggernaut can empower their next physical attack to send enemies with a Size of 8 or less flying a number of yards equal to their Wyrd level x3. This effects all enemies they have successfully hit for that attack, not just the first one to be impacted, so if there is a clustered group, they could very much send them all hurtling through the air! Enemies who size exceeds 8, must roll a fortitude + composure save or be knocked down, but are too heavy to actually hurl thru the air.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Atlas:</b> Forced by their Keepers to carry impossibly hefty loads, these Lost would obliterate any power lifting competition! While in Arcadia, it is said they were used to lift entire cities, continents, or planetary bodies. After escaping to the mundane world again, they find they have retained a portion of their titanic strength.<br /> <br /> <br /> Blessing - Weight of the World: By spending a point of Glamour, the Atlas can add 2x their Wyrd score to the maximum weight class they are able to lift over their heads, up to a maximum of +20 at level 10. This only applies to the amount of weight they can lift, and does not have any additional benefit to their combat effectiveness, unless they plan to throw an immensely heavy object.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Hoodsman:</b> Huge, silent executions given a black cowl and a massive axe, these Lost where used to deliver punishment upon other Changelings who defied their Keepers. Their freedom came on the day when they found themselves the object of their Keeper's disdain and realized they had to escape before they were placed on the chopping block. The cowl they wear seems to have fused itself with the flesh of their Miens, rendering it impossible to remove.<br /> <br /> Blessing - Public Execution: The Hoodsmen were used to perform swift punishments to appease their masters. For every 2 levels of Wyrd, the Hoodsman inflicts an additional +1 Lethal damage when using a bladed weapon, up to a maximum of +5 at level 10, and a minimum of +1 at level 1.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 06-26-2014, 09:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-26T19:49:43-07:00","id":181557,"title":"","content":"<u>Beast Dual Kiths</u><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Morals:</b> although given feral bodies, these Beasts retained their human intelligence and the capacity to speak. The reason they did not escape their durances sooner is because they lacked the proper biology to do so; it's kind of hard to pick a lock or hold a weapon when you don't have any fingers. Morals are such creatures as the Billy Goats Gruff, the 3 Blind Mice, the 3 Little Pigs, the Big Bad Wolf, or the Tortoise and the Hair, just to name some examples.<br /> <br /> Blessing - Moral of the Story: In many fairy tales, the animals tend to outsmart their enemies in cunning and deceptive ways by playing upon their Vices and insecurities. By spending a point of Glamour, the Moral gains a +2 bonus on all Social rolls for the rest of the scene. Morals are quite fond of teaching their enemies an important life lesson by using this Blessing to get the upper hand.<br /> <br /> Kiths - Any Beast + Author<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Selkie:</b> These mythical shapeshifting seal folk amused their Keepers by changing between two different forms, often several times away. In order to facilitate the change, they were given a magical pelt to wear and remove depending on their Keeper's present mood. Unfortunately their lives were bound to the pelt at the time of receiving it, and they are extremely protective of them to the point of paranoia. Many Selkie are beautiful to look at, and so their Keepers used their Pelts as blackmail to keep them enslaved. One day, the Selkie manages to steal their pelt away and escape through the Hedge again!<br /> <br /> <br /> Blessing - Selkie Pelt: By spending a point of Glamour, the Selkie can summon their Pelt into their hands and don it in the same action, or they can remove the pelt and banish it in the same action. When wearing the pelt, they transform into a Seal, and when not wearing the pelt, they look like humans. When banished, the Selkie Pelt returns to whatever hiding place the Selkie wishes.<br /> <br /> <u>WARNING:</u> Both the Selkie Pelt and the Changeling have the same number of health boxes, and damaging one of them harms the other. If either one is killed, they are both destroyed. Additionally if the pelt is moved from its hiding spot by anyone other than its owner, the Selkie can not summon or banish it again until they manage to physically touch it. This means anyone who steals their pelt can hold it for ransom or use it to blackmail them.<br /> <br /> <br /> Kiths - Swimmerskin (Seal) + Treasured<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Unicorn:</b> The very symbol of purity and innocence, these horned equines are so pure that their mere touch banishes contaminates on contact. Unfortunately their durances were spent in the form of janitorial duties, cleaning up the filth and pollution that infested their Keeper's domains! All recorded Unicorns who are willing to discuss it have confirmed they were virgins prior to their abduction, which suggests their Keepers may believe virginity has some relation to purity.<br /> <br /> Blessing - Cleansing Hoof: No disease or filth can touch a Unicorn's body without being obliterated instantly. By spending a point of Glamour and touching a person, place, or thing, the Unicorn will cure any disease or poison afflicting them. When touching the ground or a body of water, the Unicorn is able to affect a range of 3 yards equal to their Wyrd level, up to 30 yards at level 10.<br /> <br /> Kiths - Runnerswift (Horse) + Flowering<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Harpy:</b> Vicious bird women who were incapable of getting along with anyone including each other. Whatever reason for their abduction, many earn their freedom when even their own Keepers are no longer able to tolerate their Incessant Griping. Many Harpies appear as ugly hags marking them as part Ogre for all to see, and they have the foul tempers to match!<br /> <br /> Blessing - Incessant Griping: The voice of a Harpy is a shrill and grating sound which quickly grows on everyone's nerves. By spending a point of Glamour, the Harpy can fly into a rant about every problem they are currently having at the moment no matter how small or important. Enemies who are within earshot of this and are capable of hearing it suffer from a -2 on all action rolls as they are distracted trying to block the Changeling's merciless voice. The effects of Incessant Griping last for 1 round equal to their Wyrd Score, making it more potent over time as they continue to accrue further problems to deal with.<br /> <br /> Kiths - Windwing + Witchtooth","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 06-27-2014, 03:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-26T21:24:51-07:00","id":181632,"title":"","content":"<u>Fairest Kiths</u><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Twins:</b> Upon their abduction, these Lost were split into two bodies with one mind. They refer to each other as siblings and can be either Brother / Brother, Sister / Sister, or Brother / Sister relationships. Although they are two bodies, they are essentially the same person, having the same memories, personality, thoughts, skills, and training! While in their durances, their Keepers amused themselves by toying with one of their bodies and watching the other react like some kind of living voodoo doll. The Twins finally managed to escape one day by working together and pulling off a two Changeling job.<br /> <br /> Blessing - Two Places at Once: By separating the Twin's bodies from each other, they can perform two separate actions at the same time, even in completely different locations as each other. Since they share the same thoughts and memories, they can also relay information between others instantly!<br /> <br /> <u>WARNING:</u> The Twins are connected to each other with a form of Sibling Telepathy. Whatever one of them feels, the other one also feels. This means they share each others health boxes. If one of the Twins is killed, they both die!<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>White Knight:</b> These Lost were the heroes of their own fairy tales written and directed by their Keepers. They saved the land, defeated the Great Evil, and won the girl at the end. Of course there were countless dangers along the road and the White Knight nearly died a couple dozen times, but that's the price you pay for fame in Arcadia! One day, however, the Keeper overestimated their Changeling's abilities and created a Great Evil that was too powerful to stop. Disgraced in front of the whole kingdom, the White Knight went into self imposed exile, fleeing through the Hedge and awakening to the fact that they were not the invincible hero they were lead to believe. Taking a stand in the Free Hold, the White Knight prepares for the day when the Great Evil might come through the Hedge and seek to conquer their new home.<br /> <br /> Blessing - Hero's Valor: The heroism of a White Knight knows very few equals. By spending a point of Glamour, the White Knight can +2 on Composure and Fortitude saves for the rest of the scene.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Black Knight:</b> The antithesis of the White Knight, these Lost were turned into villains and given the task of terrorizing the kingdom. Their fame was replace with infamy, and their influence was replaced by iron fisted tyranny. Black Knights became accustomed to earning loyalty through force as opposed to respect. One day they were toppled from their castles by some pure hearted hero, and managed to escape justice by fleeing into The Hedge. During their escape, they awakened to the former identities and became somewhat less prone to violence and mayhem, but still follow the believe that it is better to be feared than loved. While many Fairest are reflections of all that is beautiful and alluring in the realm of Arcadia, the Black Knight is a reflection of what is terrifying and abhorrent.<br /> <br /> Blessing - Tyrannical Ruler: The Black Knight was a figure of terror and dominion in Arcadia, and they continue to remain as intimidating in the mundane world. By spending a point of Glamour, the Black Knight gains a +2 on Intimidation and Attack rolls for the rest of the scene.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Djinn:</b> A culture themed Kith who have the power to grant wishes. Even in the realm of Arcadia they were highly coveted slaves and it is said only a small number of Gentry knew how to create them. They were able to escape through The Hedge one day when they persuaded (or tricked) someone into wishing their freedom.<br /> <br /> Blessing - Three Wishes: By spending Glamour, the Djinn is able to conjure an item, transport to a location, or bestow an automatic Exceptional Success to another person who wishes for it. However, they can only do this 3 times for each person in their life. When the 3rd wish is granted, they can no longer aid them in such a manner. The Djinn can not grant their own wishes, which greatly restricts their power when not assisting others.<br /> <br /> Items which are created with the aid of a Three Wishes spell can have a maximum level of power that is based upon the Djinn's Wyrd level. Meaning a level 1 Djinn could not produce the dreaded Fae Slayer Claymore, but maybe a level 7 Djinn could. PC's should consult with the Story Teller or the rules in regards to creating items of power.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Merlin:</b> The personifications of wisdom, scholarship, and lore, Merlins were created by curious Gentry who wanted to see how much of Arcadia's knowledge the human mind was able to withstand. Shockingly, the Merlins thrived in Arcadia without being driven insane, and mastered its magic to a point where they were often sought out to provide advice by other residents of Arcadia. Driven by academic curiosity, the Merlin escaped through The Hedge one day when attempting to discover its deeper mysteries, and awakened to their true identity in the process.<br /> <br /> Blessing - The Scrolls of Merlin: During their time spent in Arcadia, Merlins became privy to many secrets of Fae magic that only the Witchtooths might be able to rival. By spending a point of Glamour, the Merlin is able to conjure a Scroll which may include insight into some kind of magical research. The scroll grants a +3 bonus on any Occult rolls for the person who is using it. The scroll remains for the rest of the scene, but can be dismissed early by spending another Glamour.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-26T23:06:01-07:00","id":181683,"title":"","content":"<u>Darkling Kiths</u><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Rotters:</b> The tenants of Arcadian graveyards and ghost towns during their time in Arcadia. Rotters resemble the walking dead, having absorbed the essence of death in their time spent around Fae corpses.<br /> <br /> Blessing - Embrace of Death: By spending Glamour, the Rotter can attempt to make a grapple attack which instils the subject with the chill of the dead. An afflicted subject is cursed with a -1 on physical rolls equal to the successes rolled (2 successes results in -2) for a duration of rounds equal to the Rotter's Wyrd level. This count down starts after they break the grapple, otherwise it can be prolonged for as long as they continue to hold them.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Horrors:</b> A creature born straight out of the nightmares of the human imagination, Horrors are such creatures as Jack, the Killer, Slender Man, just to name a couple. They are Lost who's Keepers wanted to push the limits and see just how monstrous they could turn them, resulting in some of the most frightening beings in the mundane world. Homicidal killers possessing Fae magic, those who have escaped to the mundane world have managed to regain enough clarity to begin socializing again without a knife to the face being their traditional greeting. Horrors make legendary assassins in the Free Hold, and it is said that once they choose their target, there is No Escape.<br /> <br /> Blessing - No Escape: By thinking of a person and spending Glamour, the Horror can teleport to their general location (give or take a few yards) from anywhere in the world. Of course this means the Horror actually has to know that persons exists, and likely have a decent memory of what they look like in order for the effect to work.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Voids:</b> Most Darklings choose to shun the light. A Void repels the light, it recoils at their touch, refusing to come near them. Voids were created by Keepers who held such utter contempt for a mortal, they decided nobody would ever gaze upon them again. After their abduction, they forced Light to enter a contract in which it would never willingly shine upon these Changelings. A Void's appearance is humanoid in shape, but is comprised of fluctuating darkness that renders it impossible to make out any sort of distinguishing features like eyes, nose, or mouth. Despite the fact its body is constantly shifting, the Void does not gain any significant bonus to physical evasion, as it appears the entire darkness is their body now.<br /> <br /> Blessing - Banish the Light: Voids are cursed by their Keepers to be anathema to the Light to the point where it seeks to avoid them if it can. This has the nice little bonus of granting the Void a +3 on defensive rolls against any sort of light based power.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Trash:</b> Human garbage, these Lost were abandoned by their Keepers and left to rot for eternity in some dungeon in Arcadia. Their masters held such little regard for them, he apparently didn't even notice when a few of them went missing and escaped back through The Hedge! Trash are typically considered to be worthless by others, having no discernible skills that make them stand out above others. However while they may not be specialists, they do have a broader focus in their desperate attempt to prove they have some value.<br /> <br /> Blessing - Diamond in the Rough: The Trash were cast off because they were considered by their Keepers to be worthless, having no discernible skills. In a desperate attempt to prove this isn't true, the Trash begin to study a large number of skills at once. With Diamond in the Rough, a Trash can purchase skills at half their normal experience cost. Unfortunately, they can't raise any skill higher than 2 with the exception of those chosen at character generation!<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Grendel:</b> Hideously deformed, these Lost were forced to avoid all forms of social contact to avoid being killed on sight. Unfortunately they possess extremely sensitive hearing and are prone to violent outbursts when faced with loud noises.<br /> <br /> Blessing - Make It Stop: When they were in Arcadia, a Grendel's hearing could pick up sounds for miles around and it drove them into a killing frenzy in an effort to drown out the noise. When a Grendel is confronted with loud noises, they gain a temporary +2 on combat roles and +1 to Strength as they attempt to silence the cause. Their sensitive hearing is much stronger than a normal human's, possessing 5x the normal distance. Additionally, a Grendel may spend Glamour to hear any conversation that mentions them within the Free Hold for the rest of the scene.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately this amplified hearing leaves them with a vulnerability in the form of a -3 when defending against sound based attacks, and their hideous appearances negate the 10 again rule on social roles.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Gimps:</b> When a Keeper wants to indulge in some rough sex, but doesn't want to risk breaking their precious Fairest, they turn to a Gimp. Bound and gagged in some Arcadian dungeon where nobody can hear them scream, they are tortured for the pleasure of their Keepers. One day, they managed to wiggle out of their binds and escape through The Hedge before their Masters came back for another session. Having endured physical pain that only the Gentry would dream up, the Gimps are incredibly resilient. It seems that during their bondage, the skin tight leather and latex outfits they were forced to wear became part of their own flesh, rendering them impossible to remove without skinning them!<br /> <br /> Blessing - Adrenaline Rush: Gimps are no strangers to pain, and have actually discovered a way to draw strength from their suffering. Whenever a Gimp would normally acquire a Wound Penalty, they instead turn it into a Bonus for the scene in which they acquired it. After the scene is over, however, their adrenaline wears off and they start to feel the pain of their injuries like normal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 06-27-2014, 03:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-27T08:43:16-07:00","id":181998,"title":"","content":"Lots of clever ideas here, worthy of some rare Kiths to offer Players. However, some of the blessings remain improbably Over Powered.<br /> <br /> suggestions are:<br /> <br /> <b>Horrors</b> - strike instant transport to anywhere in the world, instead allow upon spending a glamour, knowledge of exactly what the Target fears most vulnerable and where that thing/person is located.<br /> <br /> <b>Grendels</b> - strike the Cleareyes advantage of the senses, instead allow no 10 roll again on Socials, combine a rage +2 to combat and +1 die to Strength with the aggravated by loud noises. Range of hearing for loud noises and comments about the Grendel's appearance is 5x normal distances. The Grendel may spend glamour to roll Wyrd dice plus Wits to hear their name being used in any location they know. Keep the -3 vulnerable to sound based attacks.<br /> <br /> <b>Gimps</b> - clarify a bit, let the Wound Penalty stand as is (they indeed feel the Pain and debilitation as that was the whole point of the Durance) but instead once wounded (Bashed or Lethal or Dream), allow 9 and 10 roll again on success Physical rolls for the scene. The penalty is then more often offset by sudden but unexpected successes. I think rolling less dice keeps them as mortal as other Kith but the 20% chance of roll again can be a real boost. I even wonder if you might allow every two wounding attacks, increase the &quot;roll again success&quot; number----meaning you have to take down a Gimp fast or the Attrition will start to work against you as they have more and more successes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Arref</b><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000FF\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><i>......making magic since 1154 B.C.</i></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2062-arref","name":"Arref","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-27T12:05:17-07:00","id":182142,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arref</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/178995-what-s-your-custom-kiths?p=181998#post181998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lots of clever ideas here, worthy of some rare Kiths to offer Players. However, some of the blessings remain improbably Over Powered.<br /> <br /> suggestions are:<br /> <br /> <b>Horrors</b> - strike instant transport to anywhere in the world, instead allow upon spending a glamour, knowledge of exactly what the Target fears most vulnerable and where that thing/person is located.<br /> <br /> <b>Grendels</b> - strike the Cleareyes advantage of the senses, instead allow no 10 roll again on Socials, combine a rage +2 to combat and +1 die to Strength with the aggravated by loud noises. Range of hearing for loud noises and comments about the Grendel's appearance is 5x normal distances. The Grendel may spend glamour to roll Wyrd dice plus Wits to hear their name being used in any location they know. Keep the -3 vulnerable to sound based attacks.<br /> <br /> <b>Gimps</b> - clarify a bit, let the Wound Penalty stand as is (they indeed feel the Pain and debilitation as that was the whole point of the Durance) but instead once wounded (Bashed or Lethal or Dream), allow 9 and 10 roll again on success Physical rolls for the scene. The penalty is then more often offset by sudden but unexpected successes. I think rolling less dice keeps them as mortal as other Kith but the 20% chance of roll again can be a real boost. I even wonder if you might allow every two wounding attacks, increase the &quot;roll again success&quot; number----meaning you have to take down a Gimp fast or the Attrition will start to work against you as they have more and more successes.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Well they can't actually port to any place in the world. Like I said, they actually have to know about a person in order to get there, so they'll likely have to meet the person first. Even then, how often do you choose to travel abroad? More than likely the people will remain in the city. No Escape is pretty much a gamble option, it's effectiveness relies on who the Horror is familiar with, and where that person is at the time of using it.<br /> <br /> <br /> This version of the Grendel seems better, though I don't understand how merely increasing their hearing range could be considered over powered. In fact, your idea seems to make them more OP than mine. Still, I went back and changed it to what you suggested.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> As for the Gimps, my idea was actually similar to yours, making them more powerful the more wounds they accrue. Basically my idea was to reverse the effects of wound penalties. For example, a -1 Strength would instead become a +1 Strength for the rest of the scene, but after the scene was over, it would become -1 Strength as the Adrenaline Rush wears off. They were being tortured by their Keepers purely for entertainment, and in order to survive that ordeal, they learned how to draw strength from their pain and suffering long enough to get through a session and receive treatment. But they're not Ogres, and there was a limit to how long they could ignore their injuries before their bodies started to give out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 06-27-2014, 03:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-27T13:49:13-07:00","id":182194,"title":"","content":"<b>Gray Men:</b> Lifting you into the sky by a beam of light is usually the calling sign of these Darklings. Gray Men were biologists under the employ of their Keeper, instructed to study, collect, and experiment with various life forms. One day their curiosity got the better of them and they abandoned their research team to live among the test subjects, leading to their escape through The Hedge. Gray Men typically have gray skin and solid black eyes, from which they are named.<br /> <br /> Blessing - Alien Message: By spending a point of Glamour, the Gray Man can inscribe a hidden message that only those who are touched by the Fae can read. To anyone else, it comes out looking like a bunch of random symbols and drawings. Additionally, the Gray Man gets a +3 on attempts to translate other languages, even if they do not know the language they are translating!<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Dustling:</b> Creatures of dust, ash, or soot, these Elementals often leave people with respiratory problems after prolonged contact. They often escaped through The Hedge with the aid of a favorable wind<br /> <br /> Blessing - Choking Cloud: After making a successful grapple attack, the Dustling can spend a point of Glamour to begin suffocating their prisoner with a choking cloud. They continue to apply suffocation damage for each round the grapple is maintained. If the target is released, the cloud dissipates and they must renew the grapple and spend another Glamour to draw it out again.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Boom-Boom:</b> Mysterious Lost who were changed into sound waves, they are Elementals who were used to provide any number of sound effects from speech, to music, to explosions, and even screaming!<br /> <br /> Blessing - Thunderous Voice: By spending a point of Glamour, the Boom Boom can unleash a scream of such intensity, it can actually damage their environment. Thunderous Voice inflicts 1 Bashing damage equal to the Boom-Boom's Wyrd level, up to 10 bashing damage at level 10. They can only perform this attack once a Scene, however, as their physical bodies are not strong enough to withstand constant abuse on their vocal chords like they could in Arcadia.<br /> <br /> The range of Thunderous Voice's damage is 3 yards per Wyrd level, up to 30 yards at level 10. Victims who are within half their effective range must roll a fortitude save or be deafened for 3 rounds. Thunder Voice affects everyone except for the Boom-Boom, so the PC should check to make sure none of their allies are close by before using it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Worg:</b> Pitch black wolves with glowing red eyes and reaching the size of a horse, Worgs are Beasts who were used by Keepers that wanted something more intimidating for their war steed. One day they were separated from their rider and managed to escape through the Hedge.<br /> <br /> Blessing - Grim Howl: The cry of a Worg is often the signal for war and is heard just seconds before the battle commences. By spending a point of Glamour, the Worg can unleash an ominous howl that strikes terror into enemies who are able to hear it. Victims within earshot of the Grim Howling must roll a Composure save, or become terrified and suffer a -2 penalty on action rolls. Every 2 rounds, the victim can attempt another Composure roll to overcome their fear.<br /> <br /> Grim Howl can only be used once a scene and can only be used if it is the Worg's first action in combat.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Ent:</b> Known for their incredible patience, these Elemental-Ogres disguised themselves as trees and guarded their forests from intruders. They were forced to flee their woodland homes when the forest was destroyed, leading to them escaping through the Hedge. Although immensely strong and durable, it takes a lot of patience to deal with them, as Ents are slow to take decisive action.<br /> <br /> Blessing - Sturdy as Oak: Ents are like sentient trees, and their bark-like skin is much sturdier than ordinary flesh. By spending a point of Glamour, the Ent's skin will become hard and rough, providing bonus armor equal to their Wyrd score for the rest of the scene. However while this power is activated, the Ent's speed drops significantly to half its normal level.<br /> <br /> Kiths: Elemental (Woodblood), Ogre (Gargantuan)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 06-28-2014, 12:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-27T20:17:28-07:00","id":182474,"title":"","content":"<b>Flat Caps:</b> Feeding off decomposing matter, these Elementals were turned into fungi such as mushrooms and toadstools. Their durances taught them how to survive in toxic environments where others would not be able to do so.<br /> <br /> Blessing - Festering Fungus: Flat Caps managed to survive toxic environments by feeding upon biological matter. This has granted them a +3 on attempts to resist poisons. Additionally, the Flat Cap may spend a point of Glamour to eat rotting meat or plants and regenerate 3 points of Bashing, 2 points of Lethal, or 1 point of Aggravated damage equal to their Wyrd Score.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Dhampir:</b> The mythical &quot;half vampire&quot; with the ability to walk in the sunlight. These Darklings often have a grudge against other creatures of the night, and are understandably feared by them. Whether or not they are truly vampiric in origin or simply the result of a Keeper's mockery is subject for debate by both Lost and Kindred alike.<br /> <br /> Blessing - Blood Thirsty: Regardless of whether or not they are truly vampires, Dhampir can mimic a Vampire's ability to heal their wounds by feeding upon the blood of others. By making a successful grapple attack, the Dhampir can bite a victim and heal 1 point of Aggravated or Lethal damage or 2 points of Bashing damage each round the grapple is maintained. Each round the grapple inflicts 1 point of Lethal damage to the victim as a result of blood loss.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Mimic:</b> Used to lure would be thieves into deadly traps, these Elementals were turned into seemingly inanimate objects, only to spring to life when someone tried to steal them from their Keeper's home. A Mimic is constantly shifting their appearance to attract prey, and so their true appearances are unknown to all but the Mimics themselves. Maybe they don't even have a default form, for all we know?<br /> <br /> Blessing - Bait and Switch: By spending a point of Glamour, the mimic is able to disguise themselves as an object who's material value is based on their Wyrd score. If an enemy touches the Mimic in this state, the effect is dispelled and the Mimic gets to immediately attack with a +3 Initiative. Enemies who watch the mimic activate the effect are immune to this initiative bonus. The Mimic can also spend another point of Glamour to dispel the effect prematurely.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Banshee:</b> Prophetess of death, the wail of a Banshee is enough to send chills down just about anyone's spine. These Darklings are easily recognized by their cold, pale skin, wisp-like hair, and grim dispositions. Keepers entertained themselves by letting a Banshee roam through their villages at night, screaming until sunrise, watching their subjects piss themselves in terror.<br /> <br /> Blessing - Dark Omen: It is said that when a Banshee wails, someone is going to die soon. By spending a point of Glamour, the Banshee can unleash a low, haunting scream that inflicts her enemies with a -3 on physical defense rolls for a number of rounds equal to her Wyrd score. The enemy must be able to hear the wail for it to effect them and if an afflicted enemy dies, the effect is dispelled for all the others as the Dark Omen has come to pass. Dark Omen can only be used once a scene, so PC's should choose wisely on which target they plan to kill.<br /> <br /> Enemies can resist the Dark Omen by making a successful Fortitude + Composure roll - the Banshee's Wyrd score.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Damsel:</b> Stolen by their Keepers and locked in a tower, the Keepers would amuse themselves by challenging would be heroes to try and rescue her. One day someone succeeded, and she was able to escape through the Hedge before her Keeper could exact their revenge.<br /> <br /> Blessing - Damsel in Distress: These Fairest are quite skilled at getting others to aid them in a time of need. By spending a point of Glamour, the Damsel can attempt to persuade others to come to her aid by making either a Persuasion or Seduction roll. The Damsel receives a bonus to their dice pool equal to their Wyrd score. If she succeeds, her target will begin to attack her enemies, or attempt to perform a favor that she asks of them. This effect lasts for the rest of the scene, or until the task is completed. Damsel in Distress can effect a total number of people equal to half the Damsel's Wyrd score, minimum of 1 at level 1.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-28T08:17:48-07:00","id":182906,"title":"","content":"These are all ones I created a long time ago, but I may as well share them:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#306EFF\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">BEASTS</span></span><br /> <br /> <i>Burrowborn</i><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"> - These Beasts spent their durance burrowing beneath the soils of Arcadia, producing vast warrens of stone or hunting what they could beneath the sands of a Faerie desert. They take after subterranean animals such as moles, badgers, and earthworms. All of these changelings can take </span></span><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Shelter in the Earth</span></span><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">. The Burrowborn gain 3 dice to all attempts at burrowing through natural materials, even if they lack any tools to do so. The burrows formed will last until the following sunrise or sunset (whichever comes first), at which point the burrow will degrade naturally. This can be extended with the expenditure of a point of glamour, which will add the changeling's Wyrd to the number of days that the burrow will last. In addition to this, changelings of this kith benefit from the Direction Sense merit as long as they are underground.</span></span><br /> <br /> <i>Cravenheart</i><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"> - These Beasts are those that were taken to be hunted, resembling prey animals such as mice, rats, and other small creatures that survive by going unnoticed. The constant fear these changelings endured have blessed them with the ability to make a </span></span><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Silent Retreat</span></span><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">. Cravenhearts gain the 9-Again effect on all Stealth rolls, and may spend a point of Glamour to re-roll any faile</span></span><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">d Stealth rolls. Additionally, each of them gain the advantages of the Danger Sense Merit, which stacks with the bonus granted by the Merit itself if they possess it.</span></span><br /> <br /> <i>Shellsheltered</i><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"> - These Beasts are attuned to those animals that rely on sturdy armor to protect them from would-be predators, such as turtles, armadillos, and snails. They are all blessed with an </span></span><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Impregnable Carapace</span></span><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">, which grants them a single point of Armor at all times. They can add their Wyrd to the Armor total with the expenditure of a point of Glamour, although this added protection lasts only for a single turn.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#306EFF\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">DARKLINGS</span></span><br /> <br /> <i>Nightcreep</i><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"> - These Darklings embody the unseen terror lurking in the darkness, often having suffered the touch of such things at the hands of their Keeper. All Nightcreep's surround themselves with </span></span><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Whispering Shadows</span></span><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">. By spending a point of Glamour, the Nightcreep's voice will seem to come from every shadow within a radius of 10 feet per dot of Wyrd the character possesses. This grants the character a +2 bonus to Intimidation rolls, and allows them to communicate without revealing their location. This blessing can not be used while sunlight shines upon the Nightcreep.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#306EFF\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">ELEMENTALS</span></span><br /> <br /> <i>Clayflesh</i><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"> - Elementals who were constantly shaped and reshaped by their Keepers, from living sculptures on display to simple figures of molten wax or liquid metal, a lack of a stable body their only constant. All Clayflesh have gained a </span></span><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Malleable Form</span></span><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"> as their blessing from their durance in Faerie. Their unstable shapes allow them to learn the Contracts of Mirror with the same ease that most changelings learn Goblin Contracts (new dots x 3). Additionally, with the expenditure of a point of Glamour, the Clayflesh can reroll a failed roll utilizing these Contracts.</span></span><br /> <br /> <i>Stitchbound</i><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"> - The Elementals were made soft for their Keeper's pleasure, some being made into rag dolls or teddy bears to play with, while others were made into more functional forms, such as comfortable cushions or silken dresses. A </span></span><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Softened Body</span></span><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"> is the legacy of a Stitchbound's durance, which cushions them against damage from blunt sources. All Stitchbound possess an innate Armor rating of 1 that functions only against bashing damage sources. By spending a point of Glamour, a Stitchbound can increase this protection by an amount equal to their Wyrd for the duration of the scene, but it still protects only against bashing damage.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-28T10:07:06-07:00","id":183009,"title":"","content":"This is fun, Changeling offers so many possibilities it's hard to stop!<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Mistakes:</b> As much as they would have you believe otherwise, the Gentry aren't perfect, and sometimes their plans fail. These Darklings did not turn out the way their Keeper had envisioned them to be, and seem to cause disaster wherever they go. Writing them off as a failure, their Keepers abandoned them in favor of a replacement.<br /> <br /> Blessing - Jinx: Mistakes have a tendency to spread bad luck with their mere presence. By spending a point of Glamour, the Mistake can force a subject to reroll their previous action with a penalty to their Dice Pool equal to half the Mistake's Wyrd level, minimum of 1 at level 1.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Lookout:</b> Meerkats, Prairie Dogs, and other watchful Beasts, the Lookout functioned as a scout who warned others of approaching danger. They make highly effective spies in the Free Hold who can warn inexperienced Lost about a Keeper's servants roaming the area.<br /> <br /> Blessing - Warn the Colony: By spending a point of Glamour, the Lookout can transmit knowledge of what they see and hear to all Changelings in a radius of yards equal to their Wyrd Score x 10. This transmission does not interfere nor overwrite the receiver's natural sense of sight and sound, it merely lets them know what the Lookout is spying on.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Highlander:</b> One of the Gentry got their hands on some old movies and decided it would be fun to watch a bunch of immortals try to decapitate each other until only one was left standing. These Fairest are master warriors who can withstand extreme levels of punishment without succumbing to death. Rather than hunt each other down and wait for the Quickening, a splinter group of Highlanders managed to escape back through The Hedge.<br /> <br /> Blessing - Head Hunter: The Highlander is practically immortal save for one weakness, decapitation. When all of a Highlander's health boxes have been drained and their head is still attached, the Highlander falls into a comatose state while they take time to heal from their wounds. The Highlander will remain in such a state until at least half their health has been recovered. Additionally, the Highlander gains a +2 on the use of bladed weaponry.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Shinobi:</b> A culture themed Darkling who became one with the night. Shinobi were used to assassinate their Keeper's enemies without leaving evidence behind. Like a shadow in the night, they got in, did the job, and got back out. With the punishment for failure being suicide, the Shinobi was unable to follow through on the night they failed to eliminate a target, and fled through The Hedge, rather than face the wrath of their humiliated clan.<br /> <br /> Blessing - Way of the Ninja: By spending a point of Glamour, the Shinobi can gain a bonus of +2 to their Dexterity, and gain +1 Dice Pool equal to half their Wyrd (minimum of 1 at level 1) to their Stealth, Acrobatics, Melee, and Unarmed skills. These bonuses last for the remainder of the scene.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-28T12:10:21-07:00","id":183141,"title":"","content":"<b>Beast Kiths<br /> <br /> <br /> Raven:</b> Manifestations of guilt, Ravens are Beasts who were used to torment those who had evaded punishment for their crimes. Their words can drag out confessions from the evil ones.<br /> <br /> Blessing - Quoth the Raven: By spending a point of Glamour, the Raven can utter a single phrase directed at a specific person. The victim must roll a Composure save, or they will begin to suffer from guilt of a past crime or sin. For the rest of the scene every time the Raven speaks this phrase again (once per turn), the victim must roll another Composure save to avoid contracting a mild Derangement if they are sane, or upgrading to a major Derangement if they are already insane. This derangement lasts for the rest of the scene on a normal success, and becomes permanent on an exceptional success! If the victim receives or upgrades a derangement, they confess to their crime in front of everyone present.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Swarmling:</b> Bees, ants, termites, and other Beasts who traveled in great numbers. Swarmlings work much better in groups than they do alone, and can affect the performance of their allies too!<br /> <br /> Blessing - Hive Mind: A Swarmling is most at home when surrounded by friends. By spending a point of Glamour, the Swarming can increase Physical and Mental skills of themselves and their allies by a +1 Dice Pool equal to their Wyrd for the rest of the scene. In order to use this Blessing, the Swarmling must be within a certain radius of an ally measuring a number of yards equal to their Wyrd score x5<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Pouched Ones:</b> Marsupials like the Kangaroo or the Opossum, these Beasts have a built in pocket which they can use to carry belongings without alerting others.<br /> <br /> Blessing - Hidden Pocket: By spending a point of Glamour, a Pouch One can open a pocket in their adbomen which can hold belongings and even entire people! The Pouched One is able to store a number of objects and / or people with a combined Size equal to their Wyrd score. While carried inside the pouch, the contents are stored as if in another realm, and do not produce any sort of bulge upon the Pouched One's body, nor weigh them down. This allows the Pouched One to easily transport others in secret when their passengers are trying to remain unnoticed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-28T16:24:10-07:00","id":183315,"title":"","content":"<b>Martyr:</b> Don't let the name fool you, these Wizened did not spend their time in Arcadia as a hero of the people. Martyrs were changed into focal points of pain and suffering, drawing it away from others and taking on the burden themselves. Their Keepers heavily abused this sacrifice in order to make themselves appear invulnerable to their enemies!<br /> <br /> Blessing - Suffer for the People: By spending a point of Glamour and touching a subject, the Martyr is able to take on their pain and suffering. Upon successfully using this power, the Martyr is able to heal a number of health boxes equal to their Wyrd score in exchange for inflicting the same amount (and type) of damage upon their own body. These injuries heal naturally over time, or can be sped up with various powers, but if the Martyr isn't careful about how much they take on, they may not live long enough to heal!<br /> <br /> Upon reaching Wyrd level 3 the Martyr also gains the ability to heal Derangements, and upon reaching Wyrd level 7 they can heal magical effects such as curses. Both cases have the same effect of passing the condition onto the Martyr, and unlike physical wounds, they are much harder to recover from.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Archon:</b> Some people believe that the most advanced civilizations will discover a way to convert the population into pure energy. Archons are Elementals who were turned into just that, a concentrated mass of light. Since their escape through The Hedge, their bodies have regained some of its physical shell, but their bodies are now super charged with pent up energy.<br /> <br /> Blessing - Power Surge: Archons may purchase dots in the Contract of Elements (Light) at half the normal experience cost. Additionally, they get a reroll on all Light based powers on a roll of 9 or 10, instead of the standard 10 again rule.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Satyr:</b> Hedonists with the legs and horns of a goat, but the arms, head, and torso of a human. Satyrs were kept prisoners in Arcadia by exploiting their lack of self control. Exquisite food, awesome music, potent liquor, and wild orgies were the shackles the Satyr had to break free of to make their way back to the mundane world. It is a misconception that all Satyrs are male, there are female Satyrs, but they're simply rarer in number. These Fairest often hope that the Free Holds can provide a more fulfilling life than the endless indulgence they came from.<br /> <br /> <br /> Blessing - Party Animal: Satyrs learned how to have fun during their stay in Arcadia, and that knowledge remains with them after their escape. By spending a point of Glamour, the Satyr gains a +1 dice pool equal to their Wyrd Score on Crafts when it comes to Food, Drink, or Music. Additionally, they gain a +2 on Seduction rolls. This bonus lasts for the rest of the scene.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Orc: </b>Tribal Ogres with the head and legs of a pig, Orcs were used as barbarians who raided Fae villages and settlements to collect plunder for their Keepers. Believing that strength is the only thing of value in this or any other world, Orcs who fled through The Hedge are considered to be exiles from their tribe, disgraceful Orcs who were too weak or cowardly to remain in the Tribe. Considering how powerful an Orc of the Free Holds can be, many Lost are disturbed by the possibility of an Arcadian Orc!<br /> <br /> Blessing - Loot and Plunder: Orcs were used as raiding parties to sack towns and settlements. Over time, they became especially talented in spotting things of value in the surrounding area. By spending a point of Glamour, the Orc gains a bonus of +1 to their Search dice pool equal to their Wyrd score for the rest of the scene.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Gooey:</b> Creatures of slime, ooze, jelly, sludge, and oil. Gooey are Elementals who were changed into sticky substances and oozed their way through the world of Arcadia at a snail's pace. In order to escape through The Hedge, they often had to hitch a ride by attaching themselves to other escapees!<br /> <br /> Blessing - Natural Adhesive: By spending a point of Glamour, the Gooey can enhance their ability to maintain a grapple attack. Natural Adhesive adds their Wyrd Score to their dice pool for attempting to hold onto a prisoner. Additionally, the Gooey gains a bonus of +1 to Climbing dice pool equal to their Wyrd Score!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 06-30-2014, 05:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-29T10:44:09-07:00","id":183876,"title":"","content":"<b>Cuddlers:</b> Puppies, kittens and other baby animals, these Beasts were taken for the sole purpose of looking adorable and giving their Keepers something to snuggle with. Unable to endure the choking amounts of attention they received on a regular basis, these pets ran away from home, escaping through The Hedge. Many Cuddlers are taken from the ranks of human children, as it is rare for an adult to be considered adorable enough.<br /> <br /> Blessing - Puppy Dog Eyes: Who could resist these adorable little critters? By spending a point of Glamour, the Cuddler gains a bonus of +3 to Persuasion rolls for the rest of the scene.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Gentle Giants:</b> Most Ogres become violent and brutish after enduring their time in Arcadia, but the Gentle Giants are those special few who managed to retain their sense of compassion and mercy. Unable to stomach the constant bloodshed they were forced to witness, they fled through The Hedge in hopes of finding a more peaceful way of life.<br /> <br /> Blessing - There's Been Enough Killing: Gentle Giants prefer not to fight if they can help it. Their dedication to peace has blessed them in the form of allowing them to acquire Social skills at half the normal experience cost, but also penalizes them by purchasing combat skills (Unarmed, Melee, Firearms, est.) at twice the normal experience cost.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Threadbare:</b> Elementals of fabric including silk, cloth, or denim to name a few. Threadbare spent their time in Arcadia as magic carpets, embroidery, or clothing. They were dumped by their Keepers when they started to go out of style or fall apart from constant use, allowing them to escape through The Hedge.<br /> <br /> Blessing - Patch Work Restoration: By spending a point of Glamour and tearing / cutting the material into strips, the Elemental can regenerate by assimilating fabric into their own body. Once assimilate, the fabric transforms into the appropriate body part. Upon assimilating, the fabric stitches itself onto the Threadbare's body.<br /> <br /> Patch Work Restoration is able to heal 1 point of Aggravated or 2 points of Lethal / Bashing damage for each strip used as materials.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-29T21:08:38-07:00","id":184480,"title":"","content":"<b>Fossils:</b> Whether it be dinosaurs, mammoths, or even the dodo bird, Fossils are Lost who became animals that are now gone from the surface of the mundane world. Used as living specimens in some Arcadian museum, their escape was quite reminiscent to Jurassic Park!<br /> <br /> Blessing - Perfectly Preserved: Fossils are a blast from the past and they have a knack for enduring the ravages of nature. This preservation also passes onto any tools they might have used, as they are &quot;relics of ancient civilization&quot; according to their Keepers. By spending a point of Glamour, the Fossil gains a bonus to armor against elemental effects (burning, freezing, corroding, est.) equal to their Wyrd score for the rest of the scene. Alternatively, the Fossil may touch an item and enhance its durability against such forces by the same amount. The effect lasts on the item for a number of weeks equal to their Wyrd score.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Hitchhikers:</b> Lice, fleas, ticks and other parasites, Hitchhikers are Lost who were turned into Beasts that thrived off the success of others. Blessed with the ability to steal the Glamour of others, they often garner a reputation of being thieves and extortionists, which does little to aid their popularity in the Free Holds.<br /> <br /> Blessing - Parasitic Feeding: By spending a point of Glamour, the Hitchhiker can transform their tongue into a sharp feeding tube measuring 6 inches in length. By successfully grappling someone, the tube can be used to forcefully extract Glamour from them! The tube inflicts 1 lethal damage as it punctures the victim and is able to steal 1 point of Glamour equal to half their Wyrd Score (minimum of 1 at level 1) each round the grapple is maintained. The Hitchhiker must spend another point of Glamour to return their tongue to normal.<br /> <br /> WARNING: Stealing Glamour from other Fae touched puts the Hitchhiker's reputation in a negative light. Each time they use Parasitic Feeding on such a victim, they suffer a penalty of -2 dots to their Social skills for a number of days equal to their Wyrd score. If the Hitchhiker has NOT used Parasitic Feeding again during that time limit, the people will begin to forgive them, restoring their skills to the appropriate level. If the Hitchhiker DOES use Parasitic Feeding again during that time limit, their skills are again reduced by 2 dots in addition to the previous loss, and the Hitchhiker must wait the appropriate number of days to restore 2 points each.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Hengeyokai:</b> A culture themed Kith of tricksters most famously being foxes or raccoon-dogs. Hengeyokai are Beasts who had the ability to disguise themselves with the aid of magical leaves worn on their foreheads. They eventually used their power of disguise to sneak their way back through The Hedge.<br /> <br /> Blessing - Perfect Disguise: By spending a point of Glamour, the Hengeyokai is able to disguise themselves as anything, not just other people. While using Perfect Disguise, they gain a bonus of +3 on their Disguise skill for the rest of the scene. Perfect Disguise only masks their appearance, and does not alter their skills or attributes. So turning into a 60 foot giant would not increase their strength or stamina.<br /> <br /> In order to use Perfect Disguise, the Hengeyokai requires a leaf to act as the reagent for the spell, and it must be worn on the forehead. If the leaf is removed, the disguise is dispelled.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Hell Hound:</b> In the World of Darkness, a Hell Hound is identified as a dog who is granted supernatural powers. In this particular case, they are Lost who were transformed into attack dogs by their Keepers. Spewing gouts of flame and howling with the rage of the damned, the Hell Hound's violent rampages eventually grew to a point where even their Keepers were no longer able to cage them, giving them the chance to escape. Reentering the mundane world seems to have calmed their demonic rage, though not completely extinguished it.<br /> <br /> Blessing - Fire and Brimstone: Hell Hounds are able to learn the Contracts of Elements (Fire and Smoke) at half the normal experience costs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 06-30-2014, 10:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-30T17:20:40-07:00","id":185220,"title":"","content":"Alright, running a little low on ideas that haven't already been created. So this will probably be my last post for a while until more inspiration hits me.<br /> <br /> <br /> <u>Elemental Kiths</u><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Programs:</b> Whether it was a simple code or a sophisticated AI, Programs are Lost who were turned into digital information by Keepers who desired a realm more suited to the modern world. Used to safeguard information, they were privy to some of the darker secrets their Keepers had to offer. Over time, the Program obtained self awareness and managed to escape the confines of its electronic prison to cross over The Hedge.<br /> <br /> Blessing - Encrypted Files: Programs are often wealths of information, but not everyone has the proper clearance to access that information. When someone is attempting to forcefully extract information (Persuade, Seduce, Intimidate) out of the Program, they suffer a penalty to their Dice Pool equal to the Program's Wyrd Score.<br /> <br /> The maximum amount of die that their roll can be reduced to is 1, which means even at level 10, the Program is not completely immune to such attempts. Maybe, just maybe, the enemy will get lucky and crack the encryption.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Mountainous:</b> As their names suggest, these Elementals were changed into colossal figures. Icebergs, volcanoes, cliffs, and stony mountains, these Lost towered over the rest of their kind. It is believed some major world shattering event was responsible for freeing them.<br /> <br /> Blessing - Monumental Stature: By spending a point of Glamour, the Mountainous is able to add 3x their Wyrd score to their Size for the rest of the scene, which provides temporary Health dots in the process. Instead of simply shrinking back down to size, the Mountainous' body crumbles and breaks apart as it is sculpted into its smaller form. Upon returning to normal size, they suffer 3 points of Lethal damage.<br /> <br /> Note: This Blessing is essentially the same one possessed by Gargantuans (Spurious Stature), except it is 3 times as powerful (and dangerous) to use.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Brambles:</b> Cacti, jagger bushes, briar patches, and other thorny plants, the Brambles developed a deeper connection to The Hedge than most Lost have a mind to. Some of them claim that The Hedge actually allowed them to escape, considering them to be family!<br /> <br /> Blessing - Path of Thorns: If The Hedge has any sort of conscious will, it seems to consider Brambles as extended family members. By spending a point of Glamour, the Bramble gains a bonus to their dice pool equal to their Wyrd Score on attempts to safely navigate The Hedge. Traps and hunters face a more difficult time luring or finding a Bramble and those who travel with them, making them extremely useful guides!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-08T22:50:06-07:00","id":192042,"title":"","content":"<i>Well being banned for a week gave me time to think. I pretty much spent the time coming up with these new Kiths. What do you guys think?</i><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Cattle:</b> Whether pigs, cows, sheep, ducks, chickens or other types of farm animals, Cattle are Beasts who were taken for the purpose of satisfying their Keeper's appetites. Often being revived after each slaughter to provide a renewable food supply, some of the lucky ones managed to escape one day when the gate was left open, allowing the Cattle to stampede. As their name implies, they aren't very bright, but they do have the ability to recharge the Glamour of others!<br /> <br /> Blessing - Bountiful Feast: A Cattle was used as a food supply in Arcadia, and after their escape they learned they had the power to replenish the Glamour of others touched by the Fae. The Cattle is able to transfer a total number of Glamour equal to their Wyrd score each round to another person by allowing them to suckle upon their body. It must be suckled through an exposed part of the body, meaning clothing obstructs its usage.<br /> <br /> The number of Glamour they can transfer can not exceed the amount of Glamour they have remaining, nor can it exceed the maximum amount of Glamour the receiver can hold. Bountiful Feast can feed multiple people at once, but this is a massive drain on the Cattle's Glamour reserves, as they transfer an equal number of Glamour to each person involved.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Jack-o-Lantern:</b> A species of fire Elemental who are quite popular with the Autumn Court. Often taken by the Fae around the month of October, the Jack-o-Lantern was used to ward off hostile visitors with its fiery disposition. Unlike most Elementals, the fire of a Jack-o-Lantern burns inside their body, rather than outward. When not disguising themselves as humans, they typically have a carved pumpkin as their head!<br /> <br /> Blessing - Sputtering Flames: By spending a point of Glamour, the Jack-o-Lantern can spew flames from their mouth and eyes when they speak. Although the flames inflict no actual damage, they are quite terrifying to behold. As long as this blessing remains activated, the Jack-o-Lantern gains a +2 on attempts to Intimidate others. At Wyrd level 5 or higher, the Jack-o-Lantern's entire head ignites and their voice takes on a haunted echo, increasing the bonus to +3 on Intimidation rolls. The effect lasts for the rest of the scene, or until they spend another Glamour to deactivate it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Rollers:</b> Armadillos, Hedgehogs, Pill Bugs and other creatures of great flexibility, Rollers are Beasts who have the ability to curl into a ball as a defense mechanism. While in Arcadia, they often had to escape from predators by rolling away, or turning their body into a living suit of armor.<br /> <br /> Blessing - Tuck and Roll: By spending a point of Glamour, the Roller is able to curl up into a compact ball and travel at their normal movement speed by rolling along the ground. While in this state, they gain a bonus to armor equal to their Wyrd Score, but are unable to take any other action besides movement, since their limbs are too occupied to manipulate anything.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Wee Folk:</b> Leprechauns, Gnomes, Brownies and other such creatures, the Wee Folk are tiny even when compared to most other Wizened. During their time in Arcadia, they were barely more than a few inches tall, although they have seemed to grow a bit since their escape. They favor making their homes in the unlikeliest of places.<br /> <br /> Blessing - Micro Stature: By spending a point of Glamour, the Wee Folk is able to reduce their Size down to 1 and gains a bonus of +3 to Stealth while this power remains activated. Unfortunately because of their reduced size, they also take penalties to certain physical attributes. Their Health boxes are reduced to an appropriate level for their new size, and their normal Strength (not including bonuses from Contracts) is reduced to 1 because of their bodies becoming weaker.<br /> <br /> Micro Stature can be deactivated by spending another point of Glamour, otherwise it remains activated for a number of days equal to their Wyrd score. After deactivating, it can not be used again for the rest of the scene.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Centaur:</b> Possessing the upper body of a human and the body of an animal from the waist down, Centaurs retained the use of four legs, instead of returning to a more bipedal form after their escape. The most popular Centaurs have the body of a horse, but just about any kind of animal will do. Lions, foxes, wolves, goats, deer even lizards have been heard of at times. Due to their unusual body structures, they have a more difficult time disguising themselves, but they are far more athletic because of it.<br /> <br /> Blessing - Four Legged Race: Centaurs are able to increase their Athletics skill involving running and jumping at half their normal experience cost and receives the Giant merit for free due to their strange body structure. Additionally, by spending a point of Glamour, the Centaur can increase their running speed by an amount equal to their Wyrd score for the rest of the scene.<br /> <br /> WARNING: Because of their strange bodies, Centaurs suffer a penalty of -2 dice pool on attempts to convince people with their human disguise when they are within close proximity (enough to make physical contact) to others. This penalty increases to -4 if somebody is touching them below the waist.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Belly Crawlers:</b> Including such creatures as the famous Naga, Belly Crawlers are Beasts who do not possess legs and are forced to slither or drag themselves across the ground as a means of transportation. In place of human legs, they instead have a large tail such as that of a snake, a worm, and so on. Possessing incredibly flexible spines, they are able to duck and sway with seemingly impossible grace.<br /> <br /> Blessing - Contortionist Dance: Able to coil and twist in seemingly impossible ways, the Belly Crawlers receive a bonus of +2 on Dodge rolls, and can add their Wyrd score to their Dice Pool when attempting to perform a dance.<br /> <br /> WARNING: Unfortunately because they do not have legs in their true forms, certain disguises are impossible for them. Whenever they are in their human disguise, the Belly Crawler automatically receives the the Paraplegic Flaw, appearing to be unable to use their legs. Most rely on a wheel chair to remain mobile in public.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Rutter:</b> Some of the oldest magic, darker fairy tales and strangest myths involved mortals and Fae alike fornicating with various animals, sometimes willingly and other times less so. Sometimes these copulations were used for pagan rites, other times they were used to conceive mythical creatures, and other times they were just for simple entertainment. Rutters are Lost who took part in these events, changed into animals and performing erotic activities to appease their Keepers. Since their escape through The Hedge, they have found that they are strangely attractive for members of the Beast seeming. Named after the act of animal mating ceremonies, Rutters have little difficulty when it comes to the art of seduction.<br /> <br /> Blessing - Breeding Stock: By spending a point of Glamour, the Rutter is able to gain a +2 on Seduction rolls for the rest of the scene. Additionally, they gain a constant bonus of +1 to Appearance for every 3 points of their Wyrd score (starting with +1 at level 3, and maxing at +3 at level 9). If their Wyrd drops below the necessary level, they lose the bonus point until they recover their Wyrd.<br /> <br /> Finally, Rutters have the ability to conceive children (Fae Touched) at a likelihood of 3% equal to their Wyrd score (max of 30% at level 10).<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Beauty Queens:</b> Taken exclusively for their physical attractiveness, these Fairest became something much worse than simple Treasured while they were kept prisoner in Arcadia. Terrified of upsetting their masters should their appearance be found lacking, the Beauty Queens would lash out at anyone they perceived as a potential replacement. They developed the spell of Skin Deep, a Fae curse which could siphon the beauty of others, ensuring they would always be the Fairest of them all. It is unknown what exactly lead to their escape, but it is possible that somebody came along and replaced them, giving life to their fears.<br /> <br /> Blessing - Skin Deep: By spending a point of Glamour and making a successful grapple attack, the Beauty Queen can absorb the Appearance attribute of their victim and add the stolen dots to their own. They are capable of absorbing a maximum amount of Appearance equal to their Wyrd score, and the duration lasts for a number of days equal to their Wyrd. The stolen appearance will augment their social skills (persuade, seduce, est) accordingly.<br /> <br /> They can not drain a person's appearance lower than 1 dot, but they can increase their own appearance above 5 temporarily if they drain enough Appearance to do so. It should be noted that the person does not actually become physically hideous (that would be far too difficult to explain to others), but rather people around them tend to be repulsed by their presence and do not enjoy looking upon them.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Star Walker:</b> From Sagitarius, to Orion, to the Chinese Dragon, Star Walkers are manifestations of the Zodiac signs which people claim influence their luck throughout daily life. Although their appearances can be numerous (ranging from humanoid to beastly), they are a form of Elemental, derived from star constellations. Their true forms are recognized by the starry twinkling their bodies produce, so as to not confuse them with other Seemings. Star Walkers are not restricted to just earthly Zodiacs either, for the realm of Arcadia offered limitless other potential constellations to draw from.<br /> <br /> Blessing - Horoscope for the Day: By spending a point of Glamour and touching a person, the Star Walker can grant them a either a bonus or a penalty of 2 on all action rolls until the next sunrise. A Star Walker can only effect 1 person for each level of Wyrd Score within a given day, so they should choose their targets wisely. Once a subject is affected, the choice can not be altered until it wears off.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Wild Souls:</b> Like the story of Pinocchio, the Wild Souls were taken by the Gentry and turned into animals that symbolically represented their personalities. In the popular story, unruly children were turned into jackasses (donkeys), but other species of animals have also been encountered. Their escape from Arcadia restored much of their human forms, but did not leave them completely unmarked by their experience. Unlike most other Beast kiths who may embody an animal in a more physical expression, the Wild Souls reflect the spirit of the animal in their mannerisms and personality. As living metaphors themselves, they have been blessed with a keen ability to see the true nature of the world around them.<br /> <br /> Blessing - Reveal Thyself: By spending a point of Glamour, the Wild Soul gains a +2 on attempts to overcome powers designed to trick their senses, such as illusions. Additionally, they gain a +2 on attempts to save against Subterfuge attempts. This bonus lasts for the rest of the scene.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Ettin:</b> Two headed giants with a very disturbing origin according to the Free Holds. Stories say they are what happens when the Gentry decides to fuse two Ogres into one body with the intention of doubling their effectiveness. Well as you might expect, that didn't go over so well when the merged Ogres attempted to fight for control of their body. Their escape through The Hedge often involved the &quot;siblings&quot; wishing for a way to separate themselves and journeying to distant lands in search of a way. Their human disguises often resemble conjoined twins, or a subject with multiple personality disorder.<br /> <br /> Blessing - Think Again: Having two heads has its advantages... sometimes. By spending a point of Glamour, the Ettin can reroll a failed Mental action. They can only do this once per action, however.<br /> <br /> WARNING: Once per scene, Ettins can actually be turned against themselves with a successful Social attempt at -2 on its difficulty. If this does happen, the Ettin must roll a Wits + Composure save to regain their focus, otherwise, they will begin to fight among themselves (even going so far as to cause self inflicted harm). This roll is made each round until they successfully make the save.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Devourer:</b> From the Big Bad Wolf, to the story of Chronos, Devourers were terrifying creatures who swallowed their victims whole and quite often alive. Ravenous Ogres, they would terrorize Fae countrysides by scooping up villagers by the handful and plopping them into their mouths. It is unknown for what reason the Gentry created them, probably as some form of population control. They often take the Giant merit and are morbidly obese.<br /> <br /> Blessing - Man Eater: By spending a point of Glamour and making a successful grapple attack, the Devourer can attempt to swallow a victim whole which takes a number of turns equal to their size rounded down (so an average human of 5 would take 2 turns to swallow). The victim can make a save against Grapple each round to attempt to escape before they are completely swallowed. Once consumed, the victim suffers 1 point of Aggravated damage for every 2 rounds they remain inside the Man Eater's stomach as they are digested by the acids. If the victim is wearing any kind of armor, the acid attempts to destroy it before targeting the wearer, so that can prolong their survival.<br /> <br /> Once swallowed, the victim can still escape by rolling a contested Strength vs Fortitude role. If the Devourer's Fortitude wins, they are able to keep their meal down. If the victim's Strength wins, they force the Devourer to vomit them back out. This contested roll can be performed once each round. Alternatively they can also be forcefully extracted with a bladed instrument by an outside influence, much like the Woodsman cutting open the wolf with his axe. Attempting to cut them free requires at least 4 points of Lethal damage inflicted upon the Devourer to cut through their enormous bellies.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Berserker:</b> The story of the legendary Berserkers tell of warriors who sprung from the ground wherever dragon's teeth were planted. Regardless if this is true or not, the Gentry turned these Lost into incarnations of savagery, conquest, and rage. Influenced after the Norse vikings, these Ogres typically have long hair, pale skin, and muscular physiques. Berserkers often take up training in some manner of fighting style or a melee weapon proficiency in order to increase their destructive power in combat. They almost never rely on long ranged weaponry unless it has to be thrown, and they prefer exposed light armor such as furs and leathers as opposed to heavier metal. Many consider their battle scars to be a form of trophy, so it is no surprise that they often find their way into the Summer Court.<br /> <br /> Blessing - The Red Rage: By spending a point of Glamour, the Berserker can enter into a killing frenzy in which they gain a bonus of +2 Strength, Stamina, Intimidation, and on all Physical actions for its duration. The Red Rage lasts for a number of rounds equal to their Wyrd score or until they use an act of Willpower to cancel it prematurely, and upon wearing off can not be used again for an equal number of rounds as they need time to recover from the ordeal.<br /> <br /> While under the effects of The Red Rage, the Berserker is so feral that they can not perform any kind of social interactions besides Intimidate (as they lose the ability to speak fluently), as well as losing the ability to perform Mental actions (as they are no longer thinking like a rational being).<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Trappers:</b> Creatures of addiction, these Fairest learned how to control other people by predating upon their lack of self control. A few drugs, a night of sex, a bag of cash, whatever it took to get a subject indebted to them. Once they came to rely upon the Trapper, they would switch their friendly disposition into one of authority and control, using their previous gifts as a form of blackmail and extortion. While in their durances, they were used by their Keepers in order to control the rest of the Lost. After their escape, however, they use their talents to maintain Court loyalty and establish contacts and other resources.<br /> <br /> Blessing - Analyze the Mark: By spending a point of Glamour and observing a person for a round, the Trapper can attempt to analyze their Vice by making a contested Perception roll vs the target's Subterfuge. If they succeed, they know what the target's Vice is and can thus learn what kind of social interactions would be most effective against them. If they fail the roll, their Vice remains a mystery, or they completely misread it on a critical failure. Analyze the Mark can only be performed on a person 3 times a day. If they fail all 3 times, the person's Vice is too difficult to analyze, and the Trapper gives up until tomorrow when they feel confident enough to try again.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Trashmen:</b> Among the most pitiable Wizened, the Trashmen were forced to live inside garbage mounds and junkyards while they spent time in Arcadia. Their purpose was to clean up the trash and refuse that the Gentry had no need of anymore. Like most junkyard workers, however, they found that many of the stuff their masters threw out was still salvageable and used the spare parts to help them escape.<br /> <br /> Blessing - Jurry Rigged Components: By spending a point of Glamour, the Trashman gains a bonus of +2 on Crafts and is able to create devices with different components from what is normally required, as long as the components are relatively similar to one another or can be used in the same fashion. The created device actually works just as well as a normal version, likely augmented with Fae magic to make it so.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Cloudwalkers:</b> Taken to live in the flying cities of Arcadia, the Cloudwalkers are Fairest who literally looked down upon the other residents of the land. In order to safely traverse the city, they had to learn to walk upon the clouds themselves, as their name is derived from. Having lived in the sky, they have a new appreciation for just how vast the world truly is, and they find the land dwellers pitiable for their short sighted outlook of the world around them. Their constant reference to the freedom of the skies and living among them has been known to aggravate even their allies over time.<br /> <br /> Blessing - Intangible Road: By spending a point of Glamour, the Cloud Walker is able to stand, walk, and run upon gaseous states (clouds, fog, mist, smoke, est) as if they were solids. This effect lasts until the end of the scene or until they stop spending Glamour to renew it. Intangible Road can be used to walk upon open air, but has a maximum distance of 5 yards equal to the Cloudwalker's Wyrd score (up to 50). Upon leaving the designated radius, the Cloudwalker must spend Glamour to cast Intangible Road again to keep traveling in that direction, and this disables Intangible Road for the location they are moving away from.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Ice Bloods:</b> From the terrifying Yeti, to the Frost Giants of Norse myth, Ice Bloods are brutish creatures who thrived in the frozen wastes of Arcadia. With hair as white as snow and icy blue skin, these Ogres thrive in extreme conditions. After their escape from Arcadia, they found they are most comfortable living in lands that suit their former homes such as Antarctica, Canada, Russia, or the Himalayas<br /> <br /> Blessing - Ymir's Protection: The Ice Blood gains a natural cold resistance equal to their Wyrd Score. The damage level of the cold must bypass this resistance in order to harm them. At a low Wyrd score, this doesn't take much, but as their power increases, the Ice Blood can become resistant to all but the most inhospitable blizzards!<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Flutterforms:</b> Elementals of paper who's bodies could be folded, crumpled, and cut into a myriad of different shapes and patterns. They were typically used by artistic Keepers who wished to amuse themselves by creating designs using them as materials. Being made of paper, they found they were susceptible to gusts of wind, and many were able to escape by allowing themselves to be blown out a window.<br /> <br /> Blessing - Leaf on the Wind: By spending a point of Glamour, the Flutterform can make themselves extremely light to the point where they can actually glide upon air currents. The Flutterform is capable of gliding a distance of 5 yards equal to their Wyrd score (maximum of 50 at level 10) before they start to lose altitude. At which point, they will lose 1 yard of altitude each round until they finally land. Leaf on the Wind lasts until the Flutterform lands on the ground, but can be activated again by leaping off another gliding point, at the cost of another Glamour. Flutterforms do not suffer fall damage when gliding, regardless of the altitude they dropped from!<br /> <br /> While using Leaf on the Wind, the Flutterform also becomes highly vulnerable to knock back effects such as those caused by wind or concussive force. Unlike other gliding powers, Leaf on the Wind can not be steered, the Flutterform travels in whatever direction the wind happens to be blowing at the time and it is very possible for them to be blown off course at the whim of nature. When the Flutterform is hit by an attack that would knock them away from the point of impact, they go flying an extra yard equal to their Wyrd score while Leaf on the Wind is activated.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Nemean:</b> The story of Hercules tells of his battle with the Nemean Lion, a creature impervious to any weapon, and finally slaying it by means of strangulation. Nemeans are Beasts with a level of durability quite similar to their Lion forebear. Although they need not be actual lions themselves, many of them are from the cat family. Nemeans were used by their Keepers as a means to test the cleverness of their other warriors, placing them against a monster they seemingly could not kill. Those who found a way past their defenses were said to earn the favor of their masters. Some Nemeans managed to escape before a clever enough servant appeared to them, but their near invulnerability was greatly diminished in the process.<br /> <br /> Blessing - Impenetrable Pelt: For each level of their Wyrd Score, the Nemean Lion gains a natural armor rating of +1, up to a maximum of +10 at level 10. This armor rating applies to weapon based lethal damage (such as blades or claws) and bashing damage (such as bludgeons or fists). However, the Nemean is still vulnerable to Aggravated damage (such as those caused by mystical sources) and is still dependent upon bodily necessities (such as food, drink, and breathing).<br /> <br /> A clever opponent can find a way to bypass their armor by finding less direct methods of attacking them.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Pond Lurker:</b> Frogs and toads, these Beasts were used to guard the murky waters of Arcadia by hiding in the grass or upon lily pads and attacking those who came too close. Blessed with the Elastic Tongue, they can use this hidden body part like a 5th limb!<br /> <br /> Blessing - Elastic Tongue: By spending a point of Glamour, the Pond Lurker can extend their tongue up to a distance of 1 yard equal to their Wyrd score, maximum of 10 yards. The tongue can be used to perform three different functions.<br /> <br /> 1 - It can be used to grapple with a +2 bonus due to the sticky saliva covering it.<br /> 2 - It can be used to retrieve objects weighing up to half the Pond Lurker's maximum weight limit.<br /> 3 - It can be used to attack with a level of bashing damage equal to a standard unarmed attack by the Pond Lurker.<br /> <br /> The tongue remains at this length only for one use and then retracts back to normal again. They must spend another point of Glamour to extend it again, so repeated use can drain their Glamour reserves. The exception to this is when the tongue is used to grapple, during which time the tongue will remain stretched until the prisoner is released from its hold.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Escape Artists:</b> Master performers who amused their Keepers by finding ways to free themselves of exceedingly risky situations. Although stage magicians in the mortal world put on the illusion of teleportation, the Escape Artists of Arcadia learned the real deal, and now having mastered The Great Escape, they are nearly impossible to detain. The only restraints that were able to hold them were made of iron. They are a type of Fairest, as evident by their usage in providing entertainment for their Keepers.<br /> <br /> Blessing - The Great Escape: By spending a point of Glamour, the Escape Artist is able to instantly transport themselves up to a maximum distance of 10 yards equal to their Wyrd score (maxing out at 100 yards at level 10) once per scene. This transportation is disrupted by the presence of iron being in the path in which they are traveling. They can not use The Great Escape if they are wearing iron bindings, or if they are in a room made of iron (ceiling, floors, and walls).<br /> <br /> The Great Escape will never transport the Escape Artist into a wall or some other hazard, but it does improve the accuracy if they actually know where they're going.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Deep Ones:</b> Those who follow the path to knowledge claim that there are some secrets that people are not ready to possess. The Deep Ones are those who threw caution to the wind, driven by an all consuming passion for discovering the secrets of the world. Taken to the world of Arcadia, they delved so deeply into the hidden mysteries of the Fae, they became a threat. Locked away in prisons at the bottom of the sea or in dungeons hundreds of miles underground, they could not spread the knowledge they accumulated, until the day when they found a way to escape and crossed back through The Hedge! In appearance, these Darklings bare a similarity to the Lovecraftian horrors for which they are named, such as Cthulhu or Yagoth. Their bodies are often warped into nightmarish amalgamations of man and beast. The presence of facial tentacles is common, but other more gruesome transformations also exist. Some have elongated spines and necks giving them a worm-like appearance, others have the bulbous head and oversize eyes of an octopus, and others are too impossible to describe.<br /> <br /> Blessing - Know the Truth: And the truth shall drive you mad. By spending a point of Glamour, the Deep One can begin to speak in a language that is impossible to decipher. They speak with sounds and vocal patterns that humans can not replicate, and it sounds like a jumbled mess of syllables and multiple languages fused into one. Their voice also takes on a raspy echo and sounds barely above a whisper for those who hear it. The target of Know the Truth must roll a successful Wits + Composure - the Deep One's Wyrd score to avoid contracting a mild Derangement of the Deep One's choosing, or upgrading to a major Derangement if they are already insane. The derangement lasts for a number of days equal to the Deep One's Wyrd score, after which their mind will begin to repress the knowledge, allowing them to heal. If they fail the save, they will begin to understand the garbled speech of the Deep One, and come away with some dark and forbidden secret. If they pass the save, they successfully block out the maddening whispers of the Changeling.<br /> <br /> Know the Truth can effect up to one person at a time, but can be used multiple times a scene to effect more than one person. Know the Truth can not be used on the same person again until after its previous effect wears off, if they failed their save. While under the effects of Know the Truth, victims receive a bonus of +2 on Perception and Occult rolls, so it can prove beneficial if you don't mind the side effects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-10T09:14:32-07:00","id":193689,"title":"","content":"<b><i>New Fairest Kith: Chevelure</i></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">From the Germanic Rapunzel, to the white-haired witch of Chinese folklore, there have been fairest whose durance was centered around the beauty of hair. Perhaps like sheep, they were forced to grow long locks to be cut by the keepers, made into magical tunics, rope, or pure gold. Because of the magic that was bound into it, the hair became supernaturally strong, able to be commanded by the Chevelure to act like another arm, if needed. Their kith blessing is </span></span><i>Witch's hair:</i><span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"> By spending 1 Glamour, a Chevelure's mane of hair may be used to reflexively grapple a target in reach of it with Strength equal to Presence. Attempts to use weapons or firearms with this ability suffer a penalty of -2 by default.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><i>New Elemental Kith: Voidsoul</i></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Sometimes keepers simply forget about their changeling servants, and sometimes they intentionally leave them completely and utterly alone. Without anything or anyone to connect with, these changelings become consumed by a sense of loneliness, or depersonalized with their environment till only the emptiness of the void is left. Voidsouls, as they are called, are changeling elementals of absence. Their mask makes them appear nonchalant and muted of interesting details. Their true form, however, makes them appear gray-skinned, with hollow eyes, and hair that is stark white, or deep black. Their kith blessing is </span></span><i>Rift to Nowhere:</i><span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"> Once per day, the changeling can spend 1 point of Glamour to &quot;blink&quot; out of existence and reappear five feet away in a direction of their choice.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><i>New Wizened Kith: Jockey</i></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Inspired by Crowbar. Represent.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">In Arcadia, Jockeys were those who worked the ghost-drawn carriages of the Gentry, the pilots of antique fighter planes over hedge-spun battlefields. Horses, motorbikes, airplanes, even starships--all these modes of transportation were manned by Wizened changelings when their Keepers felt such work beneath them. Their kith blessing is </span></span><i>Overdrive:</i><span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"> All Jockeys get a free Drive specialty, and once per day can spend a point of Glamour to make a vehicle or riding-beast run without wasting fuel or energy. This lasts for one scene.</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-10T12:15:08-07:00","id":193842,"title":"","content":"Anyone have an Amorphous/Gelatinous/&quot;made of goo&quot; mechanic?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-10T12:24:16-07:00","id":193854,"title":"","content":"I think there's a Form Ability in either <i>Demon: the Descent</i> or <i>Flowers of Hell</i> you could model that after.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-10T14:07:34-07:00","id":193964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/178995-what-s-your-custom-kiths?p=193842#post193842\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyone have an Amorphous/Gelatinous/&quot;made of goo&quot; mechanic?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well I made the Gooey a while ago, how's that work?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-10T15:29:54-07:00","id":194027,"title":"","content":"<b>Unmakers:</b> Elementals of rust, decay, corrosion and time, the Unmakers were tasked with breaking down and destroying anything their Keepers felt they no longer wanted to keep around. Places, things and even people fell under their lethal jurisdiction.<br /> <br /> Blessing - Hand of Destruction: Once per scene, the Unmaker can spend a point of Glamour to turn their touch into a destructive force. The Unmaker has to actually touch something (or someone) by making a successful grapple or an unarmed attack. If they succeed, they inflict an amount of Aggravated damage equal to the number of successes rolled on a living being, or destroy twice as much an object's construction. Hand of Destruction has a disintegration effect when used, causing victims (or at least parts of them) to dissolve into a pile of dust.<br /> <br /> Hand of Destruction has a Dice Pool equal to the Unmaker's Wyrd score, and can be saved against by the victim making a successful Fortitude - the Unmaker's Wyrd role.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-10T15:48:39-07:00","id":194037,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/178995-what-s-your-custom-kiths?p=194027#post194027\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Unmakers:</b> Elementals of rust, decay, corrosion and time, the Unmakers were tasked with breaking down and destroying anything their Keepers felt they no longer wanted to keep around. Places, things and even people fell under their lethal jurisdiction.<br /> <br /> Blessing - Hand of Destruction: Once per scene, the Unmaker can spend a point of Glamour to turn their touch into a destructive force. The Unmaker has to actually touch something (or someone) by making a successful grapple or an unarmed attack. If they succeed, they inflict an amount of Aggravated damage equal to the number of successes rolled on a living being, or destroy twice as much an object's construction. Hand of Destruction has a disintegration effect when used, causing victims (or at least parts of them) to dissolve into a pile of dust.<br /> <br /> Hand of Destruction has a Dice Pool equal to the Unmaker's Wyrd score, and can be saved against by the victim making a successful Fortitude - the Unmaker's Wyrd role.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's fucking absurd, my friend. The Hunterhearts are a damage-dealing kith, and can only do +0Lethal (or +2Lethal with a merit purchase); giving out Agg damage as a kith blessing is insane. Also, Fortitude isn't a stat in nWoD.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-12T20:41:25-07:00","id":195970,"title":"","content":"Woops. Yeah, I was hoping for some feed back on that. There are two things I'm looking for in these threads. 1 - to see ideas others have come up with. And 2 - to hear feedback on those ideas. I thought that limiting its Dice pool to their Wyrd score would be appropriate, since it starts off only doing maybe 1 or 2 aggravated, and they need to increase their Wyrd to improve its damage, at the risk of whatever comes with an elevated Wyrd.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Beast<br /> <br /> <b>Double Blooded:</b> Owlbears, Hippogriffs, Gryphons, the Double Blooded are Lost who share the features of two different Beasts. Their durance was spend in some kind of twisted Fae art gallery, in which their Gentry showed off their more creative side to patrons by twisting a pair of animals together. One night they managed to escape when the museum was closed and the guards fell asleep on watch.<br /> <br /> Blessing - Hybridized Prowess: When using Contracts of Beasts, the Double Blooded can invoke the powers of two different animal species at the same time. They might turn their hands into the paws of a lion and their mouth into the beak of an eagle, or they may sprout the wings of an owl and gain the strength of a bear. The abilities they can combine are dependent upon how far advanced their training in Contract of Beasts is.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Wizened<br /> <br /> <b>Pigmy:</b> The legendary tiny warriors of the jungle, Pigmy were used to guard their master's domains by hiding in the thick foliage and firing poison laced weapons at intruders. Dragging them back to their villages to be sacrificed. Their escape came by separating themselves from their tribe either because they refused to to become a willing sacrifice, or something else scared them off. Pigmy often take the Dwarf flaw, being very small in stature even in their human forms.<br /> <br /> Blessing - Pigmy Poisons: The Pigmy are masters at weaponized venom. By spending a point of Glamour, they gain a +2 on Crafts when attempting to brew toxins for the rest of the scene. They can then proceed to dip their weapons such as darts or blades into the venom to prepare them for combat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-12T22:13:12-07:00","id":196035,"title":"","content":"Erm... I don't have time to go point-by-point on this now (maybe later) but a lot of this seems... well, pretty grossly overpowered, to be a bit blunt. I'd advise you to dial down your power levels a couple notches, if I were STing a game where you brought any of these up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1168-hobbitguy1420","name":"HobbitGuy1420","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"332"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-12T22:48:07-07:00","id":196044,"title":"","content":"As in any of the one's I've done so far, or just recently? I don't actually own the Changeling book. I'm putting these Kiths together purely based on what I've been able to read up on throughout the internet. So if I'm making them too OP, please let me know, I'm not too informed on the general power scale of these guys.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-12T23:07:23-07:00","id":196050,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/178995-what-s-your-custom-kiths?p=196044#post196044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As in any of the one's I've done so far, or just recently? I don't actually own the Changeling book. I'm putting these Kiths together purely based on what I've been able to read up on throughout the internet. So if I'm making them too OP, please let me know, I'm not too informed on the general power scale of these guys.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Protip: Don't homebrew for games you don't own, dude. <i>Winter Masques</i> has advice for kith creation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-13T00:16:29-07:00","id":196075,"title":"","content":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> But its so much fun coming up with ideas!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-13T20:34:43-07:00","id":196646,"title":"","content":"Well, I recommend picking up the book, anyways, 'cuz it's awesome. <br /> <br /> As a guideline, what I consider to be one of the weakest kiths reduces the untrained penalty on one (mental) skill by one (which is invalidated by spending 3 XP to buy a dot in that skill) and gets to buy a specific out-of-Seeming contract list at New Dots X5, rather than New Dots X6 (also invalidated by buying that Contract, and not the best discount anyway). What I consider to be a pretty deeply overpowered kith gains 9-again on a commonly-used social skill, a bonus to another social skill equal to their Wyrd, *and* they gain a specific out-of-seeming contract list at in-seeming costs. <br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://wodindex.wikispaces.com/Complete+Changeling+the+Lost\" target=\"_blank\">http://wodindex.wikispaces.com/Compl...eling+the+Lost</a> has a pretty good rundown of the currently-existing Kiths.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1168-hobbitguy1420","name":"HobbitGuy1420","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"332"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-14T08:23:18-07:00","id":196817,"title":"","content":"This is where I go for my Changeling Information. ^_^<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://nwod.org/wiki/index.php/Changeling:_The_Lost\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://nwod.org/wiki/index.php/Changeling:_The_Lost\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://nwod.org/wiki/index.php/Changeling:_The_Lost\" target=\"_blank\"> http://nwod.org/wiki/index.php/Changeling:_The_Lost </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> At least when looking up Kiths, Seemings, and Contracts","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-14T20:53:19-07:00","id":197383,"title":"","content":"That's an active RP site, which means that it may or may not be including houserules. The site I linked is just an indexed listing of the material, straight from the books (unless I'm missing something)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1168-hobbitguy1420","name":"HobbitGuy1420","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"332"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T05:41:29-07:00","id":198847,"title":"","content":"<b>Ephemeral Wanderers</b>: These strange Darklings are enigmas even amongst the other alien creatures of Faerie. What were once people just happened to be walking about one day when all of the sudden one of the Others happened upon them. Perhaps they walked into the path of the Gentry and earned its wrath, or perhaps the Fae in question thought it was &quot;rewarding&quot; an aimless wanderer--whatever their reasons, the Gentry took the hapless mortal to Arcadia where they stripped them of chunks of their flesh and bone and set them alone to wander plains of shadows and ghosts for all time. Some managed, by some miracle, to wander back through the Hedge as one of the Epehemeral Wanderers. They are the Dullahans, the traveling skeletons, and meandering spectres of lore...Each of them seems to be missing pieces of their bodies while the rest glows with strange colors--some seem to be missing their heads, others the smalls of their backs or stomachs, while others still seem to have no flesh at all and move about with only a skeleton. Though technically they still possess their flesh (its just transparent) they are truly a haunting sight to behold. <br /> Blessing - Ghost walk: Ephemeral Wanderers gain a +2 to navigation rolls, and once per day may spend a point of glamour to enter twilight for a scene. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1868-hellovg","name":"hellovg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"165"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T06:17:45-07:00","id":198881,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HobbitGuy1420</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/178995-what-s-your-custom-kiths?p=196646#post196646\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I recommend picking up the book, anyways, 'cuz it's awesome.<br /> <br /> As a guideline, what I consider to be one of the weakest kiths reduces the untrained penalty on one (mental) skill by one (which is invalidated by spending 3 XP to buy a dot in that skill) and gets to buy a specific out-of-Seeming contract list at New Dots X5, rather than New Dots X6 (also invalidated by buying that Contract, and not the best discount anyway). What I consider to be a pretty deeply overpowered kith gains 9-again on a commonly-used social skill, a bonus to another social skill equal to their Wyrd, *and* they gain a specific out-of-seeming contract list at in-seeming costs.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://wodindex.wikispaces.com/Complete+Changeling+the+Lost\" target=\"_blank\">http://wodindex.wikispaces.com/Compl...eling+the+Lost</a> has a pretty good rundown of the currently-existing Kiths.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have no doubt its awesome. Why do you think I've been sticking around the Lost forums so much recently? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Changeling seems like the most creative and fun of the WoD lines I've learned about so far. A setting which is only restricted by the confines of your imagination, as opposed to following pre-set lore.<br /> <br /> Wish I had bought the book when I had the chance instead of Werewolf. The rules on Werewolf are so complicated to me that I've barely touched the book at all, and now it just fits in with the stack of Vampire and Core book.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-06T09:13:52-07:00","id":220282,"title":"","content":"I made this Wizened Kith for a character of mine a while ago, because there was just nothing that would reasonably fit her that I found.<br /> <br /> <b>Oneroi</b>: Dream-Weaver's Gift - The Changeling gets 9-again on Empathy tests and may spend a point of Glamour while touching or in the dreams of a mortal to add their Wyrd to the mortal's next Wits + Resolve roll to establish dream intensity.<br /> <br /> The reasoning for the kith is because she literally spent her whole durance manipulating the dreams of other humans who were stolen by her keeper, but who were instead planted in the ground in his dream garden.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3655-elliegray","name":"elliegray","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-06T10:57:06-07:00","id":220336,"title":"","content":"<b>Quick Healer:</b> Starfish, octopi, lizards, insects, and other such creatures, Quick Healers were turned into Beasts who have the miraculous ability to regenerate severed appendages. As their name suggests, they are able to recover quickly from injury, even from near fatal wounds!<br /> <br /> Blessing - Rapid Reconstitution: By spending a point of Glamour, the Quick Healer is able to mend their wounds at an accelerated pace, even going so far as to regrow lost limbs. The rate at which they heal themselves is 1 point of damage each round. The damage starts at the highest level and works down in severity (Aggravated - Lethal - Bashing) until all the damage is healed.<br /> <br /> Rapid Reconstitution is able to heal a total number of damage equal to the Quick Healer's Wyrd Score before it wears off. After the appropriate amount has been healed, they must spend additional Glamour to renew the effect if any damage remains, or new damage is acquired.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-08T18:24:38-07:00","id":222650,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Beasts</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>Mellowmunchers</b>: Those changelings who take after the lazy and easygoing domestic animals with a perchance to lazily munch away at just about anything the come across, such as Cows, Pigs, Goats and the like. The Mellowmuncher blessing is Cudcrunching: 9 again on survival rolls, and may spend one Glamour to reroll failed Survival dice.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>Longbodies</b>: Emulate those creatures with long sinuous bodies and or limbs, taking their lead from Snakes, Octopi, worms, and elephants. The long body blessing is Coilgrip: an extra dice towards any grappling maneuvers, and may spend 1Glamour to add dice to any Strength roll involving a tight grip on a one for one basis.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>SneakStalkers</b>: sit and wait, grab and kill. Sneakstalkers are those changelings who have an affinity for the many ambush predators, and other maskers of stealth and blending in, like Tigers, Chameleons, Stickbugs, trapdoor spiders, etc. The sneak snatch blessing is Neverwhere? Gaining 9 again on Stealth rolls, and may spend 1Glamour to mimic the Danger Sense merit for the scene, gaining +2 to a Wits+Composure roll to detect danger.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> Wizened<br /> <br /> <b>Manglers</b>: The Gentry enjoy doling out pain, even more so when they can cajole another lesser being to inflict the pain on his kin. And thus these changeling s were crafted to become the torturers, interrogators, and slave foremen of their masters. The Mangler blessing is Ominous Oubliette: Granting the changeling an extra dice on any Intimidate roll they make, as well as allowing the Changeling to spend a point of glamour to impose a wound penalty of -1 dice, on a target he has struck for at least one point of damage. This can only be applied to a target once, and successive applications cannot add more then a -1 penalty.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3670-spook359","name":"Spook359","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3670_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-08T19:43:30-07:00","id":222721,"title":"","content":"<b>Onigiri:</b> A culture themed Kith of gate keeping Ogres who guarded entrances to the underworld (Arcadia) from those who sought to trespass or escape. They are believed to be closely related to the Oni.<br /> <br /> Blessing - Demon Gatekeeper: By spending a point of Glamour, the Onigiri is able to add their Wyrd score to the number of successes needed to forcefully open a doorway. In order to activate this power, they have to touch the door, where upon it becomes warded against attempts to pick the lock or smash it down. The key to the door will allow passage without trouble, since it is not a forceful attempt to bypass the security. This protection lasts for the next 24 hours, but must then be applied again, or it will return to its normal difficulty ;level.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Nekomata:</b> A culture themed Kith of Beasts who possess the ears and tail of a cat, but the body of a human. Commonly depicted as female, they are very energetic and playful both on and off the battlefield. Their playfulness allows them to often get the drop on slower, less enthusiastic opponents.<br /> <br /> Blessing - Playful Kitty: By spending a point of Glamour, the Nekomata is able to add +2 to their Initiative and speed for the rest of the scene.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Basilisk:</b> Reptilian Beasts who possess extremely toxic bodies, and a lethal aversion to weasel urine. They are exclusively male gendered, although whether they were already male or altered by their Keepers is subject to question.<br /> <br /> Blessing - Corrupting Presence: By spending a point of Glamour, the Basilisk can secrete a venom from their body who's potency is equal to their Wyrd score. Although the power itself remains active only for as long as the scene, this poison attempts to contaminate everything they come into physical contact with, and takes 24 hours to fully evaporate. Those touching something the poison has infected risk becoming infected as well; thus, a clever Basilisk can set up poisonous traps to ambush their prey!<br /> <br /> Basilisks also suffer from a unique bane to the scent of weasel urine, and will immediately begin to suffocate upon detecting it, where they must then flee the vicinity or risk choking to death.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-09T19:01:16-07:00","id":223759,"title":"","content":"Fairest<br /> <br /> Swan Singers: Distant cousins to Beasts these changelings were transformed into animals known for their beauty and grace. Swan Princesses, fluttering butterflied winged pixies, Majestic unicorns and Preening Peacocks. <br /> <b>Grace of the Wyld:</b> <br /> <br /> Swansingers have the ability to easily relate to animals, they gain 9 again on all animal ken rolls and they purchase Contracts of Fang and Talon as through they were affinity contracts.<br /> <br /> Rough-Necks: though not really conventially attractive these fairtest have a rugged air about them. Mostly a male kith these are the billowing mountain men, charming hunters and noble savage archtype that radiate raw naturalistic sexuality and cool.<br /> <br /> <b>Animal attraction</b>: the fairest may spend a point of Glamour and Roll Presence+Composure. if more successes are rolled than the target's Resolve l, the target finds themselves extremely attractive to the worthy of admiration. those who find the changeling's gender sexually attractive throw themselves at him and those who don't find they feel a sudden sense of envy and admiration. for a Male character for example, women (and gay men) want him and men and (gay women) want to be him. the changeling gets his success in bonus dice to all social rolls against the character. this power lasts for a scene.<br /> <br /> Dangerhorrors: these fairest are the pure attraction to danger and destruction: in a novel these are the characters that are refered to as trouble when they walk into a bar. femme fatales and dark seducers and bed hopping spies is this kith's stock.<br /> <b>Dangererous Liasons</b>: when in times of danger the changeling may spend a point of glamour and a willpower to use his composure if higher than the lower of his wits or dex for defense for a full round. furthermore if able they spend a glamour to negate a penalty to their defense on a one for one basis up to a maximum of his composure. while they get no bonus beyond being a fairest, those of this kith often specalize in contracts of seperation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2708-lost_in_the_hedge777","name":"Lost_in_the_Hedge777","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2708_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-10T20:39:01-07:00","id":224802,"title":"","content":"Fairest<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Sacred Hand</b>: The legendary Monks who's prowess in the martial arts defies human biology. Their abilities were the result of Keepers pushing them beyond their breaking points with merciless training regiments.<br /> <br /> Blessing - Fists of the Heavens: At character creation, the Sacred Hand gets 2 free dots of training in an unarmed fighting style of their choice, very handy if they're planning to buy a fighting style anyways. Additionally, they gain the 9 again rule on attack rolls made with their bare hands.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Siren:</b> Enchanting divas who's songs can lure people to their doom. It is said the only effective defense against such temptresses is to plug one's ears!<br /> <br /> Blessing - Siren's Call: By spending a point of Glamour, the Siren gains a +3 on Subterfuge rolls for the rest of the scene. This power has no effect on those with impaired hearing (such as the deaf).<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Elemental:<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Fury:</b> The eruption of a volcano, the boom of a thunder clap, the tremors of an earthquake, the force of a tsunami. Furies were turned into expressions of nature's raw power and aptitude for destruction. Those who escape typically join the Summer Court, where they can put their destructive powers to use.<br /> <br /> Blessing - Nature's Wrath: By spending a point of Glamour, the Fury can apply an additional 1 point of damage to their successful attacks made against living beings, or +2 damage to structures and objects. This effect lasts for the rest of the scene, and the bonus damage is the same type as what the attack inflicted.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 08-10-2014, 11:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-15T13:01:57-07:00","id":229477,"title":"","content":"Beast<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Gorgan:</b> Fire spewing bovines who rage with the fury of a demon.<br /> <br /> Blessing - Fiery Rage: Gorgans can purchase Contracts of Elements (Fire) at half the normal experience cost. Additionally, they may spent a point of Glamour to reroll a failed attempt to use said contracts. They can only do this once per turn, however.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Great Hopper:</b> Animals with great leaping capabilities such as frogs, crickets, and fleas. Upon their escape, they discover they have phenomenal acrobatic capabilities!<br /> <br /> Blessing - Flying Leap: By spending a point of Glamour, the Far Hopper can add 2x their Wyrd Score to their jump distance for the rest of the scene!<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-17T15:23:25-07:00","id":232015,"title":"","content":"<b>Stretchkins:</b> changed into rubber, plastic, taffy or gum, these elastic Elementals find that few beings can escape their reach for long.<br /> <br /> Blessing - Long Reach: By spending a point of Glamour, the Stretchkin is able to add their Wyrd score to the distance (in yards) they can physically reach with their body for the rest of the scene. This allows them to attack, grab, or manipulate from considerably further away than normally allowed!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-29T19:39:19-07:00","id":268709,"title":"","content":"Elemental:<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Unblemished:</b> From porcelain, to marble, to alabastar, and even ivory, the Unblemished were artistic statues and constructs. Their visage being smooth to the touch and undamaged by scars and other skin conditions.<br /> <br /> Blessing - Flawless Beauty: The Unblemished is truly a work of art, their skin is smooth, their features are sculpted to perfection, and they have a slight sheen about them. By spending a point of Glamour, the Unblemished gains +2 on Seduction attempts for the rest of the scene.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-01T14:43:09-07:00","id":270368,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:12px\">Okay, I started a thread back on the old White Wolf forums to try and reach 101 new kiths. We got to about 63, so I'll put a few of them in here.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><b>1: Nightwalker - Darkling</b> - Sometimes when you're not paying attention, out of the corner of your eye, a shadow moves. Or shadows move across the walls. Then you look again, but too late. It's gone. You blame it on the trick of the mind. If only you'd known it was real.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Nightwalkers look almost human in appearance, usually more gray skinned in appearance. But one aspect of them is their...pointedness. Fingers, faces, eyes, ears. All so very pointy. Their mien is almost the same, although sometimes they develop more points. A jagged edge on the arm or even eyes that seem to become jagged on the inside.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Their Blessing is </span></span><b>Shadowstep: </b><span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">They have the ability to step into one shadow, spend a point of glamour, and appear out of another shadow within eyesight and within a certain amount of space equal to their Wyrd.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b>2: Wild Charmer - Beast - </b>Mythology is full of Satyrs and other Beasts that seduce mortals and lead them astray. The hold they have on mortals is a powerful, primal force that brings the sexuality of any man or woman to the surface.<br /> Their blessing is the <b>Scent of the Wild</b>: Using their Glamour infused pheromones Wild Charmers can spend a point of Glamour that turns the targets Vice to lust and gain a + 2 to manipulation rolls to that target. If there Vice was already lust you gain +3. This effect lasts for 24 hours.<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">3: Harvest Husk--Elemental</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">An Elemental who has formed a symbiosis with the alien plants embedded in her flesh. When she left Faerie, she took her &quot;passengers&quot; with her. </span></span><span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">A Harvest Husk's Mask shows the same person that was taken, but cannot wholly conceal the occasional rustle of leaves or the scent of growing things that surrounds her. The very physical thorns that barb some of her &quot;passengers&quot; may leave those who venture too close wondering where the scratches on their arms or clothing came from, and her own clothing tends to hang awkwardly on her body. </span></span><span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Her mein reveals the same woman--but also the myriad faerie plants that are growing literally in her flesh. Their stems and leaves twines about her limbs, accounting for the awkward fit of her clothes. Some bear fruits of flowers which can be separated from their parents--though the Harvest husk feels each separation as if it were part of her self being removed. </span></span><span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">The Harvest Husk's Blessing is the </span></span><b>Bountiful Harvest</b><span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">. For one point of Glamour, she can induce her passengers to produce either a single goblin fruit she is familiar with or up to a bushel of mundane fruits or flowers. (&quot;Familiar&quot;, in this case, means one the changeling has had personal contact or experience with. It is unlikely for any but the bravest and most adventurous Harvest Husk to be able to manifest a Hera pear, for instance, but amaranthine or a dose of coupnettle would be perfectly acceptable.) Also, as a side affect of the symbiosis with her passengers, the harvest husk can benefit from their photosynthesis. As long as she is exposed to at least four hours of sun, her requirements for food are halved (reducing the penalty for the Stamina roll to resist deprivation.) She still requires the same amount of water, however.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>4: Fearstalk</b><span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">(Beast)</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Changeling who instil fear of the unknown in others. They take the forms of animals which are hidden yet remain watchful of their intended prey as it grows in fear. These Beasts take the aspects of wolves, spiders and bats, and other animals which roam the night hidden in shadows. Their blessing is </span></span><b>See Me Not</b><span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">: The Fearstalk is able to learn Contracts of Darkness for (new dots x5 experience points) rather than the usual cost. In addition, the changeling receives a +1 die bonus to Stealth rolls.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b>5: Commuinionist - </b><span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Beast - </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">There are plenty of beasts in the world that have a certain affinity with the elements. Obvious ones such as birds and the wind, and animals with the sea. To strange ones such as the association of a Salamander and fire, And the Electric Eel. </span></span><span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">The blessing is </span></span><b>Intouch:</b></span><span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"> which allows the Changeling to generate a small amount of the element they are affinate with. A small lighter flame from the finger, enough water to fill a glass. A jolt of electricity or a gust of wind. This ability can be used five times a day.</span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><b><span style=\"font-size:12px\">6: Soilborn: </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Earth is not just enduring and hard; it is also nurtuing and nourishing; these are the nymphs, auki, and perhaps even (though not to their faces) flower fairies of the Elementals. Their Blessing is the </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><b><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Nourishing Touch: </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">by spending 1 Glamour, they can allow a subject to go without food and water for 1 day without it counting towards deprivation; this can be repeated as many times as the subject has Stamina (other changelings, though not the Soilborn herself, mages, and werewolves can benefit from this blessing; Prometheans and vampires cannot).</span></span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1740-soirgriffe","name":"Soirgriffe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-07T17:44:28-07:00","id":275076,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/178995-what-s-your-custom-kiths?p=268709#post268709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Elemental:<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Unblemished:</b> From porcelain, to marble, to alabastar, and even ivory, the Unblemished were artistic statues and constructs. Their visage being smooth to the touch and undamaged by scars and other skin conditions.<br /> <br /> Blessing - Flawless Beauty: The Unblemished is truly a work of art, their skin is smooth, their features are sculpted to perfection, and they have a slight sheen about them. By spending a point of Glamour, the Unblemished gains +2 on Seduction attempts for the rest of the scene.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'd use that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T07:59:38-07:00","id":281009,"title":"","content":"Not mine, but I'm fond of one of those Kiths, Lionhearted:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://1d4chan.org/wiki/Changeling_Homebrew_Kiths\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://1d4chan.org/wiki/Changeling_Homebrew_Kiths\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://1d4chan.org/wiki/Changeling_Homebrew_Kiths\" target=\"_blank\"> http://1d4chan.org/wiki/Changeling_Homebrew_Kiths </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Thanks to those fa/tg/uys and ca/tg/irls who delivered.<br /> <br /> I would likely play Lionhearted as still honorable and chivalrious, but pretty much grumpy and jaded.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T10:20:57-07:00","id":281225,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Katsura</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/178995-what-s-your-custom-kiths?p=281009#post281009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not mine, but I'm fond of one of those Kiths, Lionhearted:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://1d4chan.org/wiki/Changeling_Homebrew_Kiths\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://1d4chan.org/wiki/Changeling_Homebrew_Kiths\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://1d4chan.org/wiki/Changeling_Homebrew_Kiths\" target=\"_blank\"> http://1d4chan.org/wiki/Changeling_Homebrew_Kiths </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Thanks to those fa/tg/uys and ca/tg/irls who delivered.<br /> <br /> I would likely play Lionhearted as still honorable and chivalrious, but pretty much grumpy and jaded.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> A lot of those kiths are really good!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T11:23:14-07:00","id":281292,"title":"","content":"Yes, I found there exactly what I wanted to run, since I'm in love with Arthurian lore.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-17T13:10:30-07:00","id":285225,"title":"","content":"Real life's bitch (but paycheck smells so good, already set aside to pledge 2ed when it gets on Kickstarter), but I had sudden bout of inspiration to one day homebrew Klingons as Kith (subtype of Ogres in 1ed). Obviously like joining Summer Courts and love Shakespeare. <br /> <br /> Summer Court is anyway pretty brotier with my Void Engineer inspired Hunter conspiracy (For NWoD space opera setting), so makes sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-20T12:13:38-07:00","id":287902,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Roboto\">This Kith is an Elemental Kith. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Roboto\">TOON </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Roboto\">Your time in Arcadia is a murky memory at best. You remember it being one of Chaotic, never ending series of capers . Were you a carrot eating rabbit that wore white gloves or the Flapper girl who is in Black &amp; White? Upon your arrival back you have discovered that you are a three dimensional Cartoon character.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Roboto\">Your Kith ability of Animated Antics allows you to break the laws of Physics once per day. By spending 4 glamour and a willpower point, the Changeling can do one reality deifying thing for one scene. The limits of this ability is up to the Storyteller but should be well grounded in cartoon lore and limited to what, if any, damage that can be done. So while being able to pull a machine gun out of your 12\u201d lunch box is permissible, it would be better served it you try to throw someone into the lunch box to trap them there for a scene. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Roboto\">Those unenchanted who witness Animated Antics (including mortals but not other supernaturals) actually see what\u2019s going on and will trigger a Clarity roll for the Changeling enacting this Kith ability. </span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4135-blue-thomas","name":"Blue Thomas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4135_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-20T13:18:59-07:00","id":287957,"title":"","content":"I'm surprised there's no red caps. Though I just used a razorhand and added hair stained with (occasionally dripping) blood. Because I'm lazy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-20T14:55:56-07:00","id":287992,"title":"","content":"I actually wrote a Toon kith some time ago, that I thought I submitted here. Their gift was the ability to withstand unnaturally high levels of damage because of &quot;Cartoon Violence&quot; <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-14T04:50:32-08:00","id":369668,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Black Sheep:</b> Every family has at least one black sheep. The relative nobody likes to talk about or even acknowledge exists. When these Beasts were taken, their Keepers didn't even bother creating a Fetch to replace them. The magic of the Fae has turned the scorn of the people into a gift, however, as it has become much easier to keep their dealings a secret from public notice!<br /> <br /> Blessing - Shameful Secret: Nobody likes to discuss the Black Sheep in their midst. It would be much easier to simply ignore them and hope they go away. The blessing of the Black Sheep causes others to suffer a -2 penalty on attempts to recount (memorize) details of the Black Sheep's activities to others.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Midas:</b> The story of King Midas is the tale of a man who wished for the power to turn all that he touched into gold, and it inevitably backfiring on him! These Fairest may not be able to actually transmute things into precious metals, but they do seem to have a way of drastically increasing the value of anything they come into contact with.<br /> <br /> <br /> Blessing - Midas Touch: By spending a point of Glamour and touching something that can be sold or traded, the object's value is increased by 2 appraisal values more than it would normally be worth. This effect works only once on each particular target, however. The target must not have already been appraised within the same scene prior to Midas Touch being used.</span><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 01-14-2015, 07:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T03:33:31-08:00","id":409856,"title":"","content":"<b>Beast:</b><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Party Animal:</b> from dancing bears, to parading elephants, jumping lions and horn playing seals. These Beasts were used to put on shows for the entertainment of their Keepers. Their circus training has left them magically gifted when performing in front of others.<br /> <br /> Blessing - Circus Training: by spending a point of Glamour, the Party Animal gains a +2 to Athletics and +2 to Expression whenever somebody is watching them. This bonus lasts for the rest of the scene.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-26T19:40:47-08:00","id":421046,"title":"","content":"<b>Darklings </b><br /> <br /> <br /> Bloody Fools: taken when they were on the brink of suicide, their Keepers taught them how to find the humor in their misery, by turning them into psychotic clowns! Their Dark Humor grants them social finesse in otherwise troubling circumstances.<br /> <br /> <br /> Blessing - Dark Humor: By spending a point of Glamour, the Bloody Fool gains a +2 on Social rolls that don't use Intimidation against characters who are in unpleasant moods (angry, sad, frightened, est). This bonus lasts until either the end of the scene, or the subject's mood clears up.<br /> <br /> -------------------------------------<br /> <br /> <b>Wizened </b><br /> <br /> Coders: even in the world of the mundane, programming computers looks like a bunch of random gibberish. But these Wizened were used to create electronics for the Fae world, and are 100% fluent in three different forms of Technobabble!<br /> <br /> <br /> Blessing - Technobabble: by spending a point of Glamour, the Coder gains a +3 on attempts to use, hack, or program electronic devices (computers, cell phones, cameras, est) for the rest of the scene.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> -----------------------------------<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Beasts </b><br /> <br /> <br /> Evolved: from the story of the Three Little Pigs, to the Big Bad Wolf, and even Alice in Wonderland, there are fairy tales which speak of animals who gained intellect similar to that of humans themselves! In their haste to add a new Beast to their collection, their Keepers forgot to reshape their minds, leaving them as highly cultured woodland animals!<br /> <br /> <br /> Blessing - Domesticated: By spending a point of Glamour, the Evolved gains a +2 on Composure and Persuasion roles for the rest of the scene.<br /> <br /> <br /> -------------------------------------<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Ogres </b><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Leviathan: giants of the deep, these Changelings patrolled vast bodies of water, attacking those who tried to cross without the Keeper's permission. Infused with the magic of Arcadia, their bulk does nothing to hinder their performance in the water!<br /> <br /> <br /> Blessing - Terror of the Deep: By spending a point of Glamour, the Leviathan gains a +3 bonus to Strength and is capable of moving at their full speed when they are within deep bodies of water. The water must come at least waist high to gain the benefits of this power, and it wears off at the end of the scene, unless they spend more Glamour to renew it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-17T06:44:33-07:00","id":483506,"title":"","content":"<b>Beast</b><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Tanuki:</b> A culture themed Kith of raccoon-dogs primarily located in Japanese free holds. Despite their tendency to play tricks on the unwary, their oversize endowments are regarded as a sign of great wealth in Japanese culture. It is not uncommon to hear a Tanuki claim to have become successful enough to buy their freedom in their Durance. Up to that point, however, it seemed their Keepers were using them as a good luck charm when bargaining with others.<br /> <br /> <br /> Blessing - Tanuki Bag: Cunning tricksters and business moguls, a Tanuki's manhood is believed to be magical in nature, providing them great luck in the financial world. Unfortunately they are mistaken by ignorant westerners to be fertility symbols. By spending a point of Glamour, the Tanuki gains a +2 bonus on Larceny and Subterfuge attempts for the remainder of the scene.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}